1
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:05,177
-♪ In the not-too-distant
future ♪

2
00:00:05,212 --> 00:00:08,318
♪ Next Sunday, AD

3
00:00:08,353 --> 00:00:11,528
♪ There was a guy named Joel

4
00:00:11,563 --> 00:00:14,497
♪ Not too different
from you or me ♪

5
00:00:14,531 --> 00:00:17,741
♪ He worked at
Gizmonic Institute ♪

6
00:00:17,776 --> 00:00:21,055
♪ Just another face
in a red jumpsuit ♪

7
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:23,747
♪ He did a good job
cleaning up the place ♪

8
00:00:23,782 --> 00:00:25,197
♪ But his bosses
didn't like him ♪

9
00:00:25,232 --> 00:00:30,030
♪ So they shot him into space

10
00:00:30,064 --> 00:00:33,205
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies

11
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:35,380
♪ The worst we can find

12
00:00:35,414 --> 00:00:36,622
♪ La-la-la

13
00:00:36,657 --> 00:00:39,349
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:39,384 --> 00:00:41,593
♪ And we'll monitor his mind

15
00:00:41,627 --> 00:00:42,870
♪ La-la-la

16
00:00:42,904 --> 00:00:45,217
♪ Now, keep in mind,
Joel can't control ♪

17
00:00:45,252 --> 00:00:47,737
♪ Where the movies
begin or end ♪

18
00:00:47,771 --> 00:00:48,910
♪ La-la-la

19
00:00:48,945 --> 00:00:51,741
♪ Because he used
those special parts ♪

20
00:00:51,775 --> 00:00:55,089
♪ To make his robot friends

21
00:00:56,711 --> 00:00:58,265
♪ Robot roll call

22
00:00:58,299 --> 00:00:59,507
-Cambot!
-Pan left!

23
00:00:59,542 --> 00:01:00,957
-Gypsy!
-Hi, girl!

24
00:01:00,991 --> 00:01:02,717
-Tom Servo!
-What a cool guy!

25
00:01:02,752 --> 00:01:04,236
-Cro-o-o-ow!
-What a wisecracker.

26
00:01:04,271 --> 00:01:07,032
-♪ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes ♪

27
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,172
♪ And other science facts

28
00:01:09,207 --> 00:01:10,518
♪ La-la-la

29
00:01:10,553 --> 00:01:13,176
♪ Then repeat to yourself,
it's just a show ♪

30
00:01:13,211 --> 00:01:16,179
♪ I should really just relax

31
00:01:16,214 --> 00:01:21,529
♪ For "Mystery Science
Theater 3000" ♪

32
00:01:23,566 --> 00:01:25,292
[Creaking]

33
00:01:25,326 --> 00:01:28,433
[Doors whooshing]

34
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,095
-30 seconds commercials time.

35
00:01:35,129 --> 00:01:36,372
-Hey, everybody.

36
00:01:36,406 --> 00:01:38,719
Um, welcome to
the Satellite of Love.

37
00:01:38,753 --> 00:01:41,377
Um, my name is Joel,and I'm marooned in outer space,

38
00:01:41,411 --> 00:01:43,793
and I guess,
in a way, uh, you are, too.

39
00:01:43,827 --> 00:01:47,072
Uh, I'm expecting a call from
the evil overlord scientists

40
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:48,901
who shot me into space
pretty soon.

41
00:01:48,936 --> 00:01:51,387
-Commercials time 
in 15 seconds.

42
00:01:51,421 --> 00:01:53,078
-So, um, stick around.

43
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,356
You know, we're going to
find out what the movie is,

44
00:01:55,391 --> 00:01:57,600
and then we're going to have
an Invention Exchange,

45
00:01:57,634 --> 00:01:59,567
and then we can get on
with the experiment,

46
00:01:59,602 --> 00:02:02,329
and then after that, I guess
you can get on with your lives.

47
00:02:02,363 --> 00:02:06,160
-Commercials time in five, 
four, three, two.

48
00:02:06,195 --> 00:02:07,161
-Don't...

49
00:02:07,196 --> 00:02:08,507
-Commercials time, now.

50
00:02:08,542 --> 00:02:11,821
-Don't go away.
We'll be right back.

51
00:02:13,063 --> 00:02:19,311
♪♪

52
00:02:19,346 --> 00:02:20,692
Okay, now, just take it easy.

53
00:02:20,726 --> 00:02:22,038
This isn't going to hurt a bit.

54
00:02:22,072 --> 00:02:24,178
-Ooh, it's going to hurt!
It's going to hurt!

55
00:02:24,213 --> 00:02:26,870
-A-Always be careful when Joel
is using the laser torch.

56
00:02:26,905 --> 00:02:27,871
All right?
-Oh!

57
00:02:27,906 --> 00:02:28,872
-See?

58
00:02:28,907 --> 00:02:30,357
Okay, look. You're -- I'm done.

59
00:02:30,391 --> 00:02:31,875
I'm done already.

60
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:34,188
I'm done. Here, okay, jump down.

61
00:02:34,223 --> 00:02:36,259
Here's your RAM chip.
Come on. There you go.

62
00:02:36,294 --> 00:02:37,364
Get out of here, now.

63
00:02:37,398 --> 00:02:39,883
Oh, my evil overlords
are calling me.

64
00:02:39,918 --> 00:02:41,195
Come in, sirs!

65
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:44,854
-Come in Joe-lene,
you pusillanimous poltroon.

66
00:02:44,888 --> 00:02:47,339
-Hey, sirs. What's going on?
What's up?

67
00:02:47,374 --> 00:02:49,203
-Well, what's up every week
at this time,

68
00:02:49,238 --> 00:02:51,378
you anti-gravitational
sewage leak?

69
00:02:51,412 --> 00:02:53,069
-It's the Invention Exchange,

70
00:02:53,103 --> 00:02:55,071
and this time, we've got
a real winner for you,

71
00:02:55,105 --> 00:02:57,694
something that'll sure to pleaseall of your frat buddies.

72
00:02:57,729 --> 00:02:59,593
-It's a little something
we like to call

73
00:02:59,627 --> 00:03:01,629
the mechanically inflating
whoopee cushion.

74
00:03:01,664 --> 00:03:03,355
As we all know,
the whoopee cushion

75
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:05,012
has been
a long-standing favorite

76
00:03:05,046 --> 00:03:06,807
among pranksters
around the world.

77
00:03:06,841 --> 00:03:07,877
[Laughs]
-Yes.

78
00:03:07,911 --> 00:03:09,844
This one has got a little twist,though.

79
00:03:09,879 --> 00:03:11,674
It's a self-inflating model,

80
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:13,848
and it's filled
with real methane gas.

81
00:03:13,883 --> 00:03:14,849
-Get the picture?

82
00:03:14,884 --> 00:03:16,920
-Larry.
-Ready?

83
00:03:16,955 --> 00:03:18,163
Whoo-hoo!

84
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:19,337
-[Coughs]

85
00:03:19,371 --> 00:03:20,786
-Excuse me. [Laughs]

86
00:03:20,821 --> 00:03:22,892
-[Sighs]
-What do you think?

87
00:03:22,926 --> 00:03:24,169
-I'm shocked.

88
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:26,240
-It's really sophomoric.

89
00:03:26,275 --> 00:03:27,690
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

90
00:03:27,724 --> 00:03:30,348
-Well, what's your little
contribution to science

91
00:03:30,382 --> 00:03:34,041
this week, Joe-lita,
my little vacuum flower?

92
00:03:34,075 --> 00:03:35,284
[Both laugh]

93
00:03:35,318 --> 00:03:37,458
-Okay, sirs.
Well, this is my new invention.

94
00:03:37,493 --> 00:03:39,253
It's called
the Cumber Bubble Bund.

95
00:03:39,288 --> 00:03:42,222
It's something you wear when youwant to make a big impression.

96
00:03:42,256 --> 00:03:44,879
Let's say it's your
first day of school somewhere,

97
00:03:44,914 --> 00:03:47,261
or you're, uh, going in
for a job interview.

98
00:03:47,296 --> 00:03:49,229
Just put on
the Cumber Bubble Bun,

99
00:03:49,263 --> 00:03:51,783
and you're an automatic
disco-dance party.

100
00:03:51,817 --> 00:03:53,888
[Whirring]
Hit the music, Cambot!

101
00:03:53,923 --> 00:03:55,718
-Prepare to go wild!

102
00:03:55,752 --> 00:03:58,238
[Dance music playing]

103
00:03:58,272 --> 00:03:59,273
-See?

104
00:03:59,308 --> 00:04:01,655
-Party, ooh, wow!

105
00:04:01,689 --> 00:04:04,174
-Okay, stop it. I got a joke.

106
00:04:04,209 --> 00:04:06,004
[Whirring continues]

107
00:04:06,038 --> 00:04:09,179
You know,champagne goes right through me.

108
00:04:09,214 --> 00:04:10,319
[Laughter]

109
00:04:10,353 --> 00:04:13,460
Anyway,
what do you think, sirs?

110
00:04:13,494 --> 00:04:15,393
-Oh, very amusing.

111
00:04:15,427 --> 00:04:16,566
-[Groans]

112
00:04:16,601 --> 00:04:21,019
-Anyway, your film today is
"Robot Monster."

113
00:04:21,053 --> 00:04:22,227
It's a classic film

114
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,505
that was nominated for
a Golden Turkey Award

115
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:27,025
for being one of
the fowl-est films ever.

116
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:28,682
-See, to call this film wretched

117
00:04:28,716 --> 00:04:31,340
would just be an insult
to the word "wretched."

118
00:04:31,374 --> 00:04:32,617
It stars no one!

119
00:04:32,651 --> 00:04:34,860
Oh, man. You won't believe this.

120
00:04:34,895 --> 00:04:37,691
-Yes, and to further
your viewing displeasure,

121
00:04:37,725 --> 00:04:42,040
we have a double-dose of that
classic Commando Cody serial

122
00:04:42,074 --> 00:04:44,214
"Radar Men from the Moon."

123
00:04:44,249 --> 00:04:46,838
Deal with it, pink boy!
-Enjoy!

124
00:04:46,872 --> 00:04:48,046
[Buzzer]

125
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,876
-Oh, movie sign!

126
00:04:50,911 --> 00:04:54,017
[Doors whooshing]

127
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:06,996
♪♪

128
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:07,997
I don't know.

129
00:05:08,031 --> 00:05:10,275
I thought that invention
was a good idea.

130
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,829
-Flaming whoopee cushion,
that was brilliant.

131
00:05:12,864 --> 00:05:15,245
-No, not that, mine,
the bubble thing.

132
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,833
-Oh, yeah. I like bubbles.

133
00:05:16,868 --> 00:05:18,110
-Look at this.

134
00:05:18,145 --> 00:05:19,836
Another one of these,
"Radar Men from the Moon."

135
00:05:19,871 --> 00:05:22,011
-Seen it.

136
00:05:22,045 --> 00:05:23,840
-Oh!
-Can we go?

137
00:05:23,875 --> 00:05:25,014
-Done it.

138
00:05:25,048 --> 00:05:27,361
-Starring the same people
as the week before,

139
00:05:27,396 --> 00:05:30,813
the week before that.
and episode after episode.

140
00:05:30,847 --> 00:05:32,021
-Hmm, yep, yep.

141
00:05:32,055 --> 00:05:33,333
-What did you do today?

142
00:05:33,367 --> 00:05:35,852
Well, we watched a stupid movie.Yeah, same as always.

143
00:05:35,887 --> 00:05:38,510
Another day in the salt mine.

144
00:05:38,545 --> 00:05:40,857
-Well,
try to keep a good attitude.

145
00:05:40,892 --> 00:05:42,376
We got to do two of these.

146
00:05:42,411 --> 00:05:43,757
-What?!

147
00:05:43,791 --> 00:05:45,862
-Oh, brother.

148
00:05:45,897 --> 00:05:48,865
-I don't think I can do that.

149
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:52,386
♪♪

150
00:05:52,421 --> 00:05:56,217
[Humming]

151
00:05:56,252 --> 00:05:59,048
Yeah. We know. We know!

152
00:05:59,082 --> 00:06:01,326
-Music is good this time.

153
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:05,330
[Dramatic music plays]

154
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,367
-"Flight to Destruction."

155
00:06:07,401 --> 00:06:09,817
Ooh, I'm quivering in my chair.

156
00:06:09,852 --> 00:06:12,337
♪♪

157
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:16,652
"Commando Cody pursues Daly and
Graber who, on Krog's orders,

158
00:06:16,686 --> 00:06:19,655
attempt to, uh,

159
00:06:19,689 --> 00:06:22,658
attempt to, uh,
bomb the rocket ship

160
00:06:22,692 --> 00:06:25,177
with Cody and the kidnapper,"
and stuff.

161
00:06:25,212 --> 00:06:28,767
-Okay, now see if you can spot
the escape scene that happens.

162
00:06:28,802 --> 00:06:30,320
We always seem to miss it

163
00:06:30,355 --> 00:06:33,979
when they get out
just before something explodes.

164
00:06:34,014 --> 00:06:36,672
♪♪

165
00:06:36,706 --> 00:06:38,536
-If I remember correctly,

166
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:41,608
they're turning onto
the bridge of death.

167
00:06:41,642 --> 00:06:45,059
♪♪

168
00:06:45,094 --> 00:06:46,371
-Hey.

169
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:49,029
Here comes Cody, and he's got
his beer goggles on.

170
00:06:49,063 --> 00:06:52,619
-He's trashed, and now
he's going to get bombed.

171
00:06:52,653 --> 00:06:55,415
-[Laughs]

172
00:06:55,449 --> 00:06:57,175
Huh?

173
00:06:57,209 --> 00:06:58,176
♪♪

174
00:06:58,210 --> 00:07:02,145
[Tires screech]

175
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:04,389
-Oh, oh, look! It's a bomb!

176
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,805
-Hey, that scene wasn't in
last time.

177
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:09,049
-That's because they didn't get
the film back

178
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:10,360
from the drugstore yet.

179
00:07:10,395 --> 00:07:13,433
-Upon further review,the refs find that Cody is dead.

180
00:07:13,467 --> 00:07:15,020
The play stands.

181
00:07:15,055 --> 00:07:16,401
Cody is dead.

182
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:20,232
♪♪

183
00:07:20,267 --> 00:07:21,510
-So the people on the Moon

184
00:07:21,544 --> 00:07:23,650
are planning a direct attack
on the world,

185
00:07:23,684 --> 00:07:26,653
soon as their saboteurs
have softened up our defenses.

186
00:07:26,687 --> 00:07:28,655
-What do you thinktheir chances are of succeeding?

187
00:07:28,689 --> 00:07:31,347
-You've seen what their ray guns
have already done here.

188
00:07:31,381 --> 00:07:33,349
If they send out a fleet
of rocket ships

189
00:07:33,383 --> 00:07:35,489
armed with atomic weapons
like those

190
00:07:35,524 --> 00:07:37,249
or perhaps even larger ones,

191
00:07:37,284 --> 00:07:40,183
it would be difficult
to hold out against them.

192
00:07:40,218 --> 00:07:41,357
-Perhaps our best move

193
00:07:41,391 --> 00:07:43,255
would be to attempt an attack
on the Moon.

194
00:07:43,290 --> 00:07:45,016
-We'd be at
a terrific disadvantage.

195
00:07:45,050 --> 00:07:46,845
I don't even see how
we could land ships there

196
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,088
in face of their ray guns.

197
00:07:48,122 --> 00:07:50,366
-We just can't sit here
and wait to be attacked.

198
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,437
-Sure we can.
We've done it a million times.

199
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,508
-Retik the Ruler told me
they plan to attack

200
00:07:54,543 --> 00:07:57,511
after their saboteurs herehave accomplished their mission.

201
00:07:57,546 --> 00:07:59,720
If we can round up
the gang operating here,

202
00:07:59,755 --> 00:08:01,135
we may stave off the attack

203
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:03,034
until we are better prepared
to meet it.

204
00:08:03,068 --> 00:08:04,069
-Yes.

205
00:08:04,104 --> 00:08:06,140
-That guy
is uglier than a mud fence.

206
00:08:06,175 --> 00:08:08,488
-You know some of the saboteurs,don't you?

207
00:08:08,522 --> 00:08:10,179
-He could make a train
dig a dirt road.

208
00:08:10,213 --> 00:08:11,456
-That is my site,

209
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:13,147
and my flying suit gives me
a considerable advantage

210
00:08:13,182 --> 00:08:14,148
in running them down.

211
00:08:14,183 --> 00:08:15,460
-Right.

212
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,979
I'll have you notifiedwhenever there's another attack.

213
00:08:17,013 --> 00:08:20,223
In the meantime, we'll put every
available man on this case.

214
00:08:20,258 --> 00:08:21,984
Goodbye, Cody.
-Goodbye, sir.

215
00:08:22,018 --> 00:08:23,330
-Bye.

216
00:08:23,364 --> 00:08:25,332
-What a nice guy.

217
00:08:25,366 --> 00:08:28,335
-Seems like a nice-enough fella.

218
00:08:28,369 --> 00:08:29,578
-At first.

219
00:08:29,612 --> 00:08:31,303
-Hey, forget about
the pearled inlay.

220
00:08:31,338 --> 00:08:32,546
Just screw it back together.

221
00:08:32,581 --> 00:08:34,824
-I'll have this ray gun finishedin a short time now,

222
00:08:34,859 --> 00:08:38,448
so you'd better arrange to get
another truck to mount it in.

223
00:08:38,483 --> 00:08:40,830
-Okay, but I'll need
some more money.

224
00:08:40,865 --> 00:08:42,349
-My purse is on the counter,
honey.

225
00:08:42,383 --> 00:08:43,833
-We'll have to sell
some more of those jewels

226
00:08:43,868 --> 00:08:45,490
you brought down from the Moon.

227
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,181
-I have only a few of them left,

228
00:08:47,216 --> 00:08:49,736
and I must keep those
for an emergency.

229
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:52,566
-What's he going to do,
luge in that outfit?

230
00:08:52,601 --> 00:08:54,534
-...your career of bank robbery.

231
00:08:54,568 --> 00:08:55,535
-Not me.

232
00:08:55,569 --> 00:08:58,261
I'm already on parole for that.

233
00:08:58,296 --> 00:09:03,612
-I know, but you would be wise
to continue to obey my orders.

234
00:09:03,646 --> 00:09:04,992
Your more recent activities

235
00:09:05,027 --> 00:09:07,477
would be of extreme interest
to the authorities.

236
00:09:07,512 --> 00:09:10,791
-Oh, who's going to report me,
you, Mr. Moon Man?

237
00:09:10,826 --> 00:09:12,793
♪♪

238
00:09:12,828 --> 00:09:15,589
-Do you need someone to help
you?

239
00:09:15,624 --> 00:09:19,144
-Yeah, but they'll have to do
the dirty work.

240
00:09:19,179 --> 00:09:20,180
-Dirty work, yeah.

241
00:09:20,214 --> 00:09:21,975
-Of course I'll go along
to check on them.

242
00:09:22,009 --> 00:09:24,494
-Very well.
Make your arrangements at once.

243
00:09:24,529 --> 00:09:25,841
Select a bank

244
00:09:25,875 --> 00:09:29,016
which is located in a
not too heavily patrolled area.

245
00:09:29,051 --> 00:09:30,328
-Like Yellowstone?

246
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:33,331
-Boy,
that guy is good at leaning.

247
00:09:33,365 --> 00:09:34,504
[Bell rings]

248
00:09:34,539 --> 00:09:37,300
Hey, his face rings a bell.

249
00:09:37,335 --> 00:09:39,475
-An MPA System bell.

250
00:09:39,509 --> 00:09:41,166
♪♪

251
00:09:41,201 --> 00:09:43,824
-Motion Picture Association?

252
00:09:43,859 --> 00:09:45,895
-It's possible.

253
00:09:45,930 --> 00:09:47,897
[Ringing continues]

254
00:09:47,932 --> 00:09:49,830
-Here they come.

255
00:09:49,865 --> 00:09:50,935
[Gunshot]

256
00:09:50,969 --> 00:09:53,558
-Oh, what a time
to get a kink in the back.

257
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:54,559
♪♪

258
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,147
He got one, too.

259
00:09:56,181 --> 00:09:58,390
Heartbreak of psoriasis.

260
00:09:58,425 --> 00:10:00,392
♪♪

261
00:10:00,427 --> 00:10:01,670
-After that car!

262
00:10:01,704 --> 00:10:04,189
-Hey, you know -- Hey,
you could get in, you know?

263
00:10:04,224 --> 00:10:06,191
There's seats for that.

264
00:10:06,226 --> 00:10:08,297
-Maybe he thinks
it's a skateboard.

265
00:10:08,331 --> 00:10:10,679
-It's a running board,
not a riding board.

266
00:10:10,713 --> 00:10:12,784
-We ought to lose them now.
We are in traffic.

267
00:10:12,819 --> 00:10:14,648
-Hey, this isn't the way
to Taco John's!

268
00:10:14,683 --> 00:10:17,271
♪♪

269
00:10:17,306 --> 00:10:19,584
-Whatever you do,
don't open your door.

270
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,690
-Oh, alone at last!

271
00:10:21,724 --> 00:10:25,383
You know, you're the man for me.

272
00:10:25,417 --> 00:10:29,283
-Gomez,
I'm not your new best friend.

273
00:10:29,318 --> 00:10:30,284
♪♪

274
00:10:30,319 --> 00:10:31,631
-Ooh, the lucky one.

275
00:10:31,665 --> 00:10:34,047
-Nice roll.

276
00:10:34,081 --> 00:10:36,049
-Oops.

277
00:10:36,083 --> 00:10:38,223
-Hey!

278
00:10:38,258 --> 00:10:39,742
♪♪

279
00:10:39,777 --> 00:10:42,883
It's John Cleese!

280
00:10:42,918 --> 00:10:45,437
-But we must have more money.

281
00:10:45,472 --> 00:10:47,992
You've got to get it somehow.

282
00:10:48,026 --> 00:10:50,408
-Not by any more bank jobs.

283
00:10:50,442 --> 00:10:52,065
-Krog is not looking good.

284
00:10:52,099 --> 00:10:54,723
-We'll have to figure out
something else.

285
00:10:54,757 --> 00:10:57,242
♪♪

286
00:10:57,277 --> 00:10:58,899
-I'll radio the Moon.

287
00:10:58,934 --> 00:11:00,729
Perhaps Retik can advise us.

288
00:11:00,763 --> 00:11:04,387
-Good idea, maybe he'll send yousome moon rocks or something.

289
00:11:04,422 --> 00:11:05,699
-He better get some shut-eye.

290
00:11:05,734 --> 00:11:07,011
-Krog, calling Retik.

291
00:11:07,045 --> 00:11:09,013
♪♪

292
00:11:09,047 --> 00:11:11,360
-Duh, nuh, nuh, nuh.

293
00:11:11,394 --> 00:11:15,053
-Meanwhile,
back at Caesar's Palace...

294
00:11:15,088 --> 00:11:17,124
-Krog, calling Retik.

295
00:11:17,159 --> 00:11:20,783
-Don't ever interrupt me while
I'm playing the nickel slots.

296
00:11:20,818 --> 00:11:22,164
-Krog, calling Retik.

297
00:11:22,198 --> 00:11:24,580
-Then stop talking
into a pine cone.

298
00:11:24,614 --> 00:11:27,238
-I have to report that
our scheme for obtaining money

299
00:11:27,272 --> 00:11:28,653
was a failure, your excellency.

300
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:30,482
-Some day it'll grow, and he'll
be talking into a tree.

301
00:11:30,517 --> 00:11:32,622
-Can you suggest some plan
that might be more successful?

302
00:11:32,657 --> 00:11:34,038
-I think I can.

303
00:11:34,072 --> 00:11:36,557
From what I hear
of activities on Earth,

304
00:11:36,592 --> 00:11:39,733
kidnapping important persons
and holding them for ransom

305
00:11:39,768 --> 00:11:41,010
has proved highly profitable.

306
00:11:41,045 --> 00:11:42,287
-It's very trendy.

307
00:11:42,322 --> 00:11:44,220
-Commando Cody, who flew
his rocket ship to the Moon,

308
00:11:44,255 --> 00:11:47,568
is very valuable to the defense
organization of his country.

309
00:11:47,603 --> 00:11:49,329
I suggest you select him.

310
00:11:49,363 --> 00:11:50,710
-An excellent idea.

311
00:11:50,744 --> 00:11:52,677
We shall carry it out at once.

312
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:54,403
-That's why he's the boss.

313
00:11:54,437 --> 00:11:58,579
-Be a rough deal, but a lotsafer than robbing another bank.

314
00:11:58,614 --> 00:11:59,822
-Of course.

315
00:11:59,857 --> 00:12:03,515
Commando Cody should be worth
at least $100,000.

316
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:04,758
-Oh, at least.

317
00:12:04,793 --> 00:12:07,347
-Shall we bring him here?
-No.

318
00:12:07,381 --> 00:12:10,143
Hire a plane and take him to...

319
00:12:10,177 --> 00:12:12,973
-Paradise City?

320
00:12:13,008 --> 00:12:17,391
Oh, not another lab fight.

321
00:12:17,426 --> 00:12:20,532
-Hey,this bra is coming along nicely!

322
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:23,018
♪♪

323
00:12:23,052 --> 00:12:29,024
-Oh, I hate to shoot a butt
like that!

324
00:12:29,058 --> 00:12:31,716
-I love that.

325
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:34,546
-Where's Cody?

326
00:12:34,581 --> 00:12:36,514
-Right over there.

327
00:12:36,548 --> 00:12:39,344
-Huh?
-Works every time.

328
00:12:39,379 --> 00:12:40,829
-[Chuckles]

329
00:12:40,863 --> 00:12:47,076
♪♪

330
00:12:47,111 --> 00:12:49,458
-Yeah, well,
that's for Enrico Fermi!

331
00:12:49,492 --> 00:12:52,392
-It is a good thing
scientists can really fight.

332
00:12:52,426 --> 00:12:55,015
They must have been
taking classes.

333
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:56,016
♪♪

334
00:12:56,051 --> 00:12:57,500
-Loose stool.

335
00:12:57,535 --> 00:13:00,849
-If I told you once,
I told you a thousand times.

336
00:13:00,883 --> 00:13:03,368
We're not rounding off pi
to four!

337
00:13:03,403 --> 00:13:05,405
♪♪

338
00:13:05,439 --> 00:13:09,340
-You MIT guys
think you're pretty tough.

339
00:13:09,374 --> 00:13:11,583
-That's for Madam Curie!

340
00:13:11,618 --> 00:13:14,586
♪♪

341
00:13:14,621 --> 00:13:17,451
-She's so cute
when she's passed out.

342
00:13:17,486 --> 00:13:18,936
-Ew.
-Geronimo!

343
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:20,454
♪♪

344
00:13:20,489 --> 00:13:22,456
Oh, right in the test tubes!

345
00:13:22,491 --> 00:13:27,910
♪♪

346
00:13:27,945 --> 00:13:31,362
-What's the physics
of a broken jaw, college boy?

347
00:13:31,396 --> 00:13:35,366
Are you referring to
the mandible or the maxilla?

348
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:37,368
♪♪

349
00:13:37,402 --> 00:13:40,543
-Yeah, tell your friends
Crick and Watson.

350
00:13:40,578 --> 00:13:43,132
-I've got a headache this big.

351
00:13:43,167 --> 00:13:45,548
-Ooh!

352
00:13:45,583 --> 00:13:50,450
-Dropped him like a bad habit.

353
00:13:50,484 --> 00:13:54,212
♪♪

354
00:13:54,247 --> 00:13:56,180
-Now will you tell us
where Cody is?

355
00:13:56,214 --> 00:13:57,767
-In Wyoming?
-I don't know.

356
00:13:57,802 --> 00:14:00,218
-Why don't we grab her
and use her to trap Cody?

357
00:14:00,253 --> 00:14:03,152
-I amgrabbing her.
-That's an idea.

358
00:14:03,187 --> 00:14:05,672
On your way, sister.

359
00:14:05,706 --> 00:14:06,673
♪♪

360
00:14:06,707 --> 00:14:08,640
Wait a minute.

361
00:14:08,675 --> 00:14:12,127
♪♪

362
00:14:12,161 --> 00:14:16,200
-At least she got to bring
her clutch purse.

363
00:14:16,234 --> 00:14:18,443
-I think it's alligator.

364
00:14:18,478 --> 00:14:21,067
It's very nice, very stylish.

365
00:14:21,101 --> 00:14:24,898
[Engine revs]

366
00:14:24,933 --> 00:14:28,419
♪♪

367
00:14:28,453 --> 00:14:32,009
-Is she double-dating again?

368
00:14:32,043 --> 00:14:34,494
Well, they seem like
nice-enough fellas.

369
00:14:34,528 --> 00:14:36,185
-At first!
-At first!

370
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:38,705
♪♪

371
00:14:38,739 --> 00:14:41,121
-How many times
do I have to tell them?

372
00:14:41,156 --> 00:14:42,536
No kickball in the lab!

373
00:14:42,571 --> 00:14:44,366
-Those same two men
who wrecked the ray gun,

374
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,436
they came after you.

375
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:47,024
-Where's Joan?
-I don't know.

376
00:14:47,058 --> 00:14:48,646
Maybe they took her with them.

377
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:51,821
-Two men and a woman drove away
from here just as I came in.

378
00:14:51,856 --> 00:14:54,031
They were too far away
to be recognized,

379
00:14:54,065 --> 00:14:55,964
but it must have been them.

380
00:14:55,998 --> 00:14:57,551
-They must have Joan.

381
00:14:57,586 --> 00:14:59,381
They're taking her
to the San Diego Zoo.

382
00:14:59,415 --> 00:15:01,176
-Police headquarters.

383
00:15:01,210 --> 00:15:02,798
-Calling all cars.

384
00:15:02,832 --> 00:15:04,317
Calling all cars.

385
00:15:04,351 --> 00:15:06,975
Be on the lookout
for two men and a babe.

386
00:15:07,009 --> 00:15:11,393
May be armed with a gigantic
experimental brassiere.

387
00:15:11,427 --> 00:15:13,326
You know what to do --

388
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:16,708
Strap it on and parade around
singing show tunes.

389
00:15:16,743 --> 00:15:18,503
-[Sneezes]
-Bless you.

390
00:15:18,538 --> 00:15:20,678
-Whoa, sund.-You're not supposed to do that.

391
00:15:20,712 --> 00:15:22,991
-That stirred up my ROMs
real bad.

392
00:15:23,025 --> 00:15:24,509
[Tires screech]

393
00:15:24,544 --> 00:15:26,201
-Okay, I'll tell him.

394
00:15:26,235 --> 00:15:27,857
The police found out

395
00:15:27,892 --> 00:15:29,342
that the car
went to the eastside airport,

396
00:15:29,376 --> 00:15:31,275
and a man took off with Joan
on a chartered plane.

397
00:15:31,309 --> 00:15:32,690
They left
just a few minutes ago.

398
00:15:32,724 --> 00:15:34,174
-If I'm lucky, I can catch them.

399
00:15:34,209 --> 00:15:36,694
-What about the bra?

400
00:15:36,728 --> 00:15:38,040
-Window!
-Window!

401
00:15:38,075 --> 00:15:39,766
-Window, hey!
-Look out!

402
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:40,767
-Whew!

403
00:15:40,801 --> 00:15:44,357
-Jack-O'-Lantern, private eye.

404
00:15:44,391 --> 00:15:46,497
-Nipple, nipple, tweak, tweak.

405
00:15:46,531 --> 00:15:48,775
-Oh!
-Fly!

406
00:15:48,809 --> 00:15:52,710
♪♪

407
00:15:52,744 --> 00:15:55,368
-Can I offer you some peanuts?

408
00:15:55,402 --> 00:15:57,887
♪♪

409
00:15:57,922 --> 00:16:03,031
-I hope they show this movie
on that flight.

410
00:16:03,065 --> 00:16:07,932
♪♪

411
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,555
-So do you like my plane, honey?

412
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:14,559
-Here I come to save the dame.

413
00:16:14,594 --> 00:16:16,147
-Hello?

414
00:16:16,182 --> 00:16:17,804
-She sees him.

415
00:16:17,838 --> 00:16:22,084
♪♪

416
00:16:22,119 --> 00:16:24,569
-Don't get excited, sister.

417
00:16:24,604 --> 00:16:26,675
I'll take care of him.

418
00:16:26,709 --> 00:16:29,505
♪♪

419
00:16:29,540 --> 00:16:33,026
-Wow, he can fly and shoot
at the same time?

420
00:16:33,061 --> 00:16:34,786
He must be ambidextrous.

421
00:16:34,821 --> 00:16:38,135
-Boy, I'd give my right arm
to be ambidextrous.

422
00:16:38,169 --> 00:16:40,413
♪♪

423
00:16:40,447 --> 00:16:41,621
-Oh.

424
00:16:41,655 --> 00:16:43,726
-She's so cute
when she's knocked out.

425
00:16:43,761 --> 00:16:45,038
-Oh, Cody is shooting.

426
00:16:45,073 --> 00:16:46,971
Hey, wasn't there something
in the rule book

427
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:50,664
about, uh, equal
and opposite reactions, Joel?

428
00:16:50,699 --> 00:16:54,185
♪♪

429
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,118
-Darn.

430
00:16:56,153 --> 00:17:01,054
♪♪

431
00:17:01,089 --> 00:17:04,989
-Ouch, that's hot!

432
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:09,856
Commando Soprano.

433
00:17:09,890 --> 00:17:18,278
♪♪

434
00:17:18,313 --> 00:17:21,316
Oh, steering is out!

435
00:17:21,350 --> 00:17:23,663
-Saves weight.

436
00:17:23,697 --> 00:17:28,116
♪♪

437
00:17:28,150 --> 00:17:29,945
-Oh, nice guy.

438
00:17:29,979 --> 00:17:32,810
♪♪

439
00:17:32,844 --> 00:17:35,847
-He ditched her.

440
00:17:35,882 --> 00:17:39,334
♪♪

441
00:17:39,368 --> 00:17:42,544
-Just like Karen Black.

442
00:17:42,578 --> 00:17:44,442
-Where's Charlton Heston
when you need him?

443
00:17:44,477 --> 00:17:46,651
-They should really work up
this act for air shows.

444
00:17:46,686 --> 00:17:47,652
It would really fly.

445
00:17:47,687 --> 00:17:50,172
[Chuckles]
-Hi, honey!

446
00:17:50,207 --> 00:17:52,623
Come die with me!

447
00:17:52,657 --> 00:17:55,695
-Hey, deplane, deplane!

448
00:17:55,729 --> 00:17:58,318
-Boss! [Chuckles]

449
00:17:58,353 --> 00:18:01,908
-He wrecked the controls!

450
00:18:01,942 --> 00:18:05,118
-Why don't you put it down
over there by those rocks?

451
00:18:05,153 --> 00:18:07,120
[Engine roaring]

452
00:18:07,155 --> 00:18:12,056
♪♪

453
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:13,816
-Bang.

454
00:18:13,851 --> 00:18:17,303
You don't have to wait
until next week.

455
00:18:17,337 --> 00:18:19,581
-Nice parking.

456
00:18:19,615 --> 00:18:29,591
♪♪

457
00:18:29,625 --> 00:18:33,008
♪♪

458
00:18:33,042 --> 00:18:35,666
-This is great,
back-to-back thrills.

459
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:39,014
-Yeah,
try to cope with it, you guys.

460
00:18:39,048 --> 00:18:41,327
-Hey, it's a new character!

461
00:18:41,361 --> 00:18:43,639
-No,
it's the same old character.

462
00:18:43,674 --> 00:18:44,813
-It said, "New."

463
00:18:44,847 --> 00:18:47,678
-Just think of it
as getting a booster shot

464
00:18:47,712 --> 00:18:50,612
twice in the same day
by the same doctor.

465
00:18:50,646 --> 00:18:52,027
-Yeah, Dr. Mengele.

466
00:18:52,061 --> 00:18:53,028
-Right.

467
00:18:53,062 --> 00:18:54,167
-Doesn't the Geneva Convention

468
00:18:54,202 --> 00:18:56,100
have rules
against this sort of thing?

469
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:58,689
-You know, I think I'm going to
go cut an apple in half

470
00:18:58,723 --> 00:18:59,690
and watch it brown.

471
00:18:59,724 --> 00:19:01,140
-I think I'll go with.

472
00:19:01,174 --> 00:19:02,969
-Hey, Servo, let's ditch him.

473
00:19:03,003 --> 00:19:04,798
-Yeah!

474
00:19:04,833 --> 00:19:07,284
-Oh, you guys, come on.

475
00:19:07,318 --> 00:19:09,976
Cut that out.
Get back here, you.

476
00:19:10,010 --> 00:19:11,943
-Hey, you can't make me.

477
00:19:11,978 --> 00:19:15,119
You can't make me.
You can't make me.

478
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,810
-Get back here, you.

479
00:19:16,845 --> 00:19:17,846
Crow?
-All right.

480
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,468
I'll sit here -- not.
-I'm hiding.

481
00:19:19,503 --> 00:19:20,607
-Come on. Ow!

482
00:19:20,642 --> 00:19:22,161
Get back over here.

483
00:19:22,195 --> 00:19:23,990
You get --
-Ow, ow, ow!

484
00:19:24,024 --> 00:19:26,165
-Tom Servo, stop it!

485
00:19:26,199 --> 00:19:27,442
You come back here.
You understand?

486
00:19:27,476 --> 00:19:28,857
-You can't make me.
You can't make me.

487
00:19:28,891 --> 00:19:30,169
-There.

488
00:19:30,203 --> 00:19:32,274
-This is Buddhist.

489
00:19:32,309 --> 00:19:35,001
You create us to suffer.

490
00:19:35,035 --> 00:19:38,177
-Aw, Crow, get back over here.

491
00:19:38,211 --> 00:19:40,662
-"Commando Cody
in his flying suit,"

492
00:19:40,696 --> 00:19:43,009
blah, blah, blah,
blah, blah, blah, blah.

493
00:19:43,043 --> 00:19:48,842
-I'm surrounded by idiots
of my own design.

494
00:19:48,877 --> 00:19:57,265
♪♪

495
00:19:57,299 --> 00:19:58,507
-Goodbye, pretty lady.

496
00:19:58,542 --> 00:20:00,923
Enjoy your in-flight meal,
baked Alaska.

497
00:20:00,958 --> 00:20:02,960
[Laughs]

498
00:20:02,994 --> 00:20:06,481
♪♪

499
00:20:06,515 --> 00:20:07,758
You know,they should work at an air show.

500
00:20:07,792 --> 00:20:10,209
Huh? Psych!
-Ow.

501
00:20:10,243 --> 00:20:16,042
♪♪

502
00:20:16,076 --> 00:20:18,217
-Nice climbing.

503
00:20:18,251 --> 00:20:20,978
-He wrecked the controls!

504
00:20:21,012 --> 00:20:24,119
-Whoa.

505
00:20:24,153 --> 00:20:25,638
-Get into that parachute.

506
00:20:25,672 --> 00:20:26,708
-Parachute?

507
00:20:26,742 --> 00:20:28,986
There was no parachute
in the last reel.

508
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:31,471
♪♪

509
00:20:31,506 --> 00:20:32,990
-Look at that.

510
00:20:33,024 --> 00:20:36,235
It looks like the little lady
is having the time of her life.

511
00:20:36,269 --> 00:20:39,238
-Shoot.

512
00:20:39,272 --> 00:20:45,520
♪♪

513
00:20:45,554 --> 00:20:48,247
-Oh. Well, there goes the model.

514
00:20:48,281 --> 00:20:49,903
What about the real plane?

515
00:20:49,938 --> 00:20:51,905
♪♪

516
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:55,530
-I'm beginning to think
these endings are rigged.

517
00:20:55,564 --> 00:20:57,842
-Oof, that was worse than usual.

518
00:20:57,877 --> 00:20:58,843
-I got her!

519
00:20:58,878 --> 00:21:01,467
I got her! Come to papa.

520
00:21:01,501 --> 00:21:03,641
Oops!

521
00:21:03,676 --> 00:21:05,678
-Hey, this is fun!

522
00:21:05,712 --> 00:21:07,196
Watch this! Wee!

523
00:21:07,231 --> 00:21:08,853
Wa-wee! [Chuckles]

524
00:21:08,888 --> 00:21:11,373
It's like a big balloon.

525
00:21:11,408 --> 00:21:13,893
♪♪

526
00:21:13,927 --> 00:21:15,688
-What became of that man?

527
00:21:15,722 --> 00:21:17,414
-He must have landed
somewhere near here.

528
00:21:17,448 --> 00:21:19,519
If you're sure you're all right,I'll look for him.

529
00:21:19,554 --> 00:21:20,693
-Well, of course I am.

530
00:21:20,727 --> 00:21:22,522
I'll walk over to the road.
-Okay.

531
00:21:22,557 --> 00:21:23,661
-Okay, let me just, uh...

532
00:21:23,696 --> 00:21:24,766
Okay, yeah. That's right.

533
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:29,495
Nipple, nipple, and fly!

534
00:21:29,529 --> 00:21:32,014
♪♪

535
00:21:32,049 --> 00:21:35,880
-What a fantastic man!

536
00:21:35,915 --> 00:21:37,710
Ah, it's been a good day.

537
00:21:37,744 --> 00:21:39,712
I'd better head towards
the highway now.

538
00:21:39,746 --> 00:21:42,577
Where is that highway?
Where am I?

539
00:21:42,611 --> 00:21:44,579
♪♪

540
00:21:44,613 --> 00:21:46,339
-You'd think he'd have
an inflated ego.

541
00:21:46,374 --> 00:21:48,721
-Or at least inflamed tissue.

542
00:21:48,755 --> 00:21:53,381
-Here is Chaz wearing his Armanifrom the desert wear collection.

543
00:21:53,415 --> 00:21:56,245
-For goons on the go.

544
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,558
-Hey, uh, you call for
a murder car?

545
00:21:58,593 --> 00:21:59,559
No, thanks.

546
00:21:59,594 --> 00:22:01,250
I already got one.
-Yeah, hop in.

547
00:22:01,285 --> 00:22:10,536
♪♪

548
00:22:10,570 --> 00:22:12,883
-He's switching
to the light-rock station.

549
00:22:12,917 --> 00:22:16,231
♪♪

550
00:22:16,265 --> 00:22:18,923
-The moon-rock station.

551
00:22:18,958 --> 00:22:19,993
-Yeah.

552
00:22:20,028 --> 00:22:20,994
♪♪

553
00:22:21,029 --> 00:22:23,376
-He flies better than Superman!

554
00:22:23,411 --> 00:22:28,899
♪♪

555
00:22:28,933 --> 00:22:30,694
-The man that flies
is chasing us.

556
00:22:30,728 --> 00:22:33,282
Step on it!
-Huh, are you crazy?

557
00:22:33,317 --> 00:22:35,146
-Don't argue. Step on it!

558
00:22:35,181 --> 00:22:36,389
-Oh,
he could've never have known

559
00:22:36,424 --> 00:22:39,392
he was picking up a Moon goon,
poor guy.

560
00:22:39,427 --> 00:22:41,290
-Right, right, shoot him.

561
00:22:41,325 --> 00:22:43,707
That's your solution
to everything.

562
00:22:43,741 --> 00:22:47,296
Something gets in your way,
you pull out your little gun,

563
00:22:47,331 --> 00:22:48,297
and you got to shoot him.

564
00:22:48,332 --> 00:22:49,713
Well, listen, mister.

565
00:22:49,747 --> 00:22:52,647
Someday there's going to be
a flying rocketeer behind you

566
00:22:52,681 --> 00:22:54,821
who's going to shoot back.

567
00:22:54,856 --> 00:22:55,822
[Gunshot]

568
00:22:55,857 --> 00:22:57,790
♪♪

569
00:22:57,824 --> 00:22:59,792
[Gunshots]
-Whoa!

570
00:22:59,826 --> 00:23:01,621
-Hey, you winged him!

571
00:23:01,656 --> 00:23:03,865
Better get out the dogs.

572
00:23:03,899 --> 00:23:05,660
-That stopped him.

573
00:23:05,694 --> 00:23:08,973
-What's the limit on Codys
this year, anyway?

574
00:23:09,008 --> 00:23:12,011
-When you shoot down a Cody,
do you call a ranger,

575
00:23:12,045 --> 00:23:15,394
or do you call
an air traffic controller?

576
00:23:15,428 --> 00:23:18,604
-It's gutting him
that's the hard part.

577
00:23:18,638 --> 00:23:20,191
Oh, darn.

578
00:23:20,226 --> 00:23:23,678
I just got this back
from the garage.

579
00:23:23,712 --> 00:23:26,197
♪♪

580
00:23:26,232 --> 00:23:29,062
-Meanwhile, back in the bowels
of the Earth...

581
00:23:29,097 --> 00:23:30,788
-We must report to the Moon.

582
00:23:30,823 --> 00:23:34,516
-I think we've all reported tothe Moon at one time or another.

583
00:23:34,551 --> 00:23:36,035
♪♪

584
00:23:36,069 --> 00:23:37,381
-Krog, calling Retik.

585
00:23:37,416 --> 00:23:44,388
♪♪

586
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:46,459
-Retik?
-Krog, calling Retik.

587
00:23:46,494 --> 00:23:47,978
♪♪

588
00:23:48,012 --> 00:23:52,914
-Retik, pick up line one please,Mr. Retik.

589
00:23:52,948 --> 00:23:54,433
♪♪

590
00:23:54,467 --> 00:23:56,400
-He's Retik and waiting.
-Come in, Krog.

591
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:58,954
-I have to report another
failure, your excellency.

592
00:23:58,989 --> 00:24:00,991
We were unable
to capture Commando Cody

593
00:24:01,025 --> 00:24:02,475
and hold him for ransom.

594
00:24:02,510 --> 00:24:04,235
-You still have no funds?

595
00:24:04,270 --> 00:24:05,858
-No, sir.-Apply for an arts grant, quick.

596
00:24:05,892 --> 00:24:07,342
-...get a ray gun
into action again,

597
00:24:07,376 --> 00:24:09,171
we are unable
to continue our campaign

598
00:24:09,206 --> 00:24:10,863
against Earth's defenses.

599
00:24:10,897 --> 00:24:12,451
-Listen carefully, Krog.

600
00:24:12,485 --> 00:24:16,213
I cannot have my preparations
for invading the Earth delayed

601
00:24:16,247 --> 00:24:17,663
by such a minor detail

602
00:24:17,697 --> 00:24:19,975
as obtaining
a small amount of money.

603
00:24:20,010 --> 00:24:23,496
If the men you now have cannot
accomplish this simple mission,

604
00:24:23,531 --> 00:24:26,050
then hire someone
who can produce results.

605
00:24:26,085 --> 00:24:29,191
This is an order!
-I understand, your excellency.

606
00:24:29,226 --> 00:24:31,021
-Hmm, hire someone else.

607
00:24:31,055 --> 00:24:34,680
I wonder if Kelly
has a thug department.

608
00:24:34,714 --> 00:24:36,682
♪♪

609
00:24:36,716 --> 00:24:37,821
-You heard?

610
00:24:37,855 --> 00:24:39,857
It's up to you to decide

611
00:24:39,892 --> 00:24:44,034
whether you can still be useful
to us or...

612
00:24:44,068 --> 00:24:46,139
-Or I forgot my line.
-We'll figure something out.

613
00:24:46,174 --> 00:24:48,556
-We'll figure out something,
if we could only use our arms!

614
00:24:48,590 --> 00:24:51,041
-Remember that payroll job Duke
was trying to get you in on?

615
00:24:51,075 --> 00:24:53,699
Maybe he'll still
go through with it.

616
00:24:53,733 --> 00:24:54,700
♪♪

617
00:24:54,734 --> 00:24:56,218
-Well?

618
00:24:56,253 --> 00:24:58,220
-It's risky, but it might work.

619
00:24:58,255 --> 00:25:00,982
It's the Western
Wholesale Supply Company.

620
00:25:01,016 --> 00:25:02,535
-Mm-hmm.

621
00:25:02,570 --> 00:25:04,468
-They keep their payroll in the
office safe every Friday night.

622
00:25:04,503 --> 00:25:06,159
There's a man in the office
who knows the combination.

623
00:25:06,194 --> 00:25:09,231
-Every time he talks,
the scene fades out.

624
00:25:09,266 --> 00:25:12,338
-Meanwhile,
further along in the script...

625
00:25:12,372 --> 00:25:14,340
[Bell ringing]

626
00:25:14,374 --> 00:25:16,411
Well, no one has been shot yet.

627
00:25:16,445 --> 00:25:17,999
It's going pretty well.

628
00:25:18,033 --> 00:25:21,554
-I think they got that car
at Getaway Rentals.

629
00:25:21,589 --> 00:25:24,074
[Ringing continues]

630
00:25:24,108 --> 00:25:25,351
[Whistle blowing]

631
00:25:25,385 --> 00:25:28,561
-It's a cop. Get going!

632
00:25:28,596 --> 00:25:32,013
-Be on the lookout
for a 1935 murder car,

633
00:25:32,047 --> 00:25:34,015
smart looker, priced to move.

634
00:25:34,049 --> 00:25:36,569
You'll be the hit
of your neighborhood.

635
00:25:36,604 --> 00:25:38,329
Owned by a little old lady.

636
00:25:38,364 --> 00:25:41,850
1935 Porter,
that's my mother dear.

637
00:25:41,885 --> 00:25:44,439
Helps me through
everything I do,

638
00:25:44,473 --> 00:25:47,649
and I'm so glad she's here.

639
00:25:47,684 --> 00:25:51,032
-That's a stunning
Jerry van Dyke.

640
00:25:51,066 --> 00:25:55,864
-You know, uh, Jerry van Dyke
has a bumper sticker that says,

641
00:25:55,899 --> 00:25:58,039
"My other car is my mother."

642
00:25:58,073 --> 00:26:00,628
-Oh, he's a nut.

643
00:26:00,662 --> 00:26:02,146
[Tires screech]

644
00:26:02,181 --> 00:26:06,806
-You're watching
the All Car Chase Network.

645
00:26:06,841 --> 00:26:08,877
[Tires screech]

646
00:26:08,912 --> 00:26:10,879
♪♪

647
00:26:10,914 --> 00:26:14,227
-All cars, all chases,
all the time.

648
00:26:14,262 --> 00:26:23,236
♪♪

649
00:26:23,271 --> 00:26:25,411
♪♪

650
00:26:25,445 --> 00:26:27,171
-They're getting closer.

651
00:26:27,206 --> 00:26:28,759
-Shoot, shoot, shoot.

652
00:26:28,794 --> 00:26:32,383
It's everyone's answer
to everything in this film.

653
00:26:32,418 --> 00:26:33,522
♪♪

654
00:26:33,557 --> 00:26:35,663
-Hey, that's my lunch!

655
00:26:35,697 --> 00:26:40,909
♪♪

656
00:26:40,944 --> 00:26:42,393
[Gunshot]

657
00:26:42,428 --> 00:26:45,327
[Gunshots]

658
00:26:45,362 --> 00:26:47,398
♪♪

659
00:26:47,433 --> 00:26:50,712
-Well, that was a nice shot.

660
00:26:50,747 --> 00:26:54,405
-I suppose he tried to do that.

661
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:58,893
♪♪

662
00:26:58,927 --> 00:27:00,653
-Meanwhile,
back at the Cody Institute

663
00:27:00,688 --> 00:27:02,793
for Scientists
Who Get Pummeled...

664
00:27:02,828 --> 00:27:05,382
♪♪

665
00:27:05,416 --> 00:27:08,143
-Honey, I'm home.
-Finally got a break!

666
00:27:08,178 --> 00:27:09,938
They called me down
to the jail hospital to see

667
00:27:09,973 --> 00:27:11,664
if I could identify a prisoner,

668
00:27:11,699 --> 00:27:13,045
and he turned out
to be one of those two

669
00:27:13,079 --> 00:27:14,633
who'd been making
all the trouble for us.

670
00:27:14,667 --> 00:27:15,944
-Well, how did they catch him?

671
00:27:15,979 --> 00:27:17,912
-Well, he and another man
staged a payroll robbery.

672
00:27:17,946 --> 00:27:19,223
-Uh-huh.

673
00:27:19,258 --> 00:27:20,673
-The police went after them,
and their car crashed.

674
00:27:20,708 --> 00:27:22,675
The other man was killed, but
our pal was only banged a bit.

675
00:27:22,710 --> 00:27:24,159
-See the dartboard up there,
you guys?

676
00:27:24,194 --> 00:27:25,298
-What did you find out
about him?

677
00:27:25,333 --> 00:27:26,334
-He was, uh, banged up a little.

678
00:27:26,368 --> 00:27:28,992
-Hey, cool.
-I'm going to get it.

679
00:27:29,026 --> 00:27:31,891
I got this giant dart.
-Don't do it, Joel.

680
00:27:31,926 --> 00:27:34,687
You'll ruin the screen!
-Come on.

681
00:27:34,722 --> 00:27:35,826
-No, don't, Joel!
-Okay. All right.

682
00:27:35,861 --> 00:27:37,517
Just an idea.

683
00:27:37,552 --> 00:27:39,865
-We might be overheard.

684
00:27:39,899 --> 00:27:42,005
-But aren't they going to try
and find out something?

685
00:27:42,039 --> 00:27:43,523
-Yes.

686
00:27:43,558 --> 00:27:45,698
They're going to move him under
guard to a private sanitarium,

687
00:27:45,733 --> 00:27:46,803
where we can question him

688
00:27:46,837 --> 00:27:48,839
without any danger
of the story leaking out

689
00:27:48,874 --> 00:27:50,910
and throwing the whole country
into a panic.

690
00:27:50,945 --> 00:27:53,430
-When will that be?
-Probably this afternoon.

691
00:27:53,464 --> 00:27:54,673
Henderson is going to
let me know

692
00:27:54,707 --> 00:27:55,812
as soon
as they make arrangements

693
00:27:55,846 --> 00:27:56,847
for having him transferred.

694
00:27:56,882 --> 00:27:59,022
I'd like you to go with me, Ted.-Sure.

695
00:27:59,056 --> 00:28:03,302
-Great! If I stay around here,
I'll get my butt kicked again.

696
00:28:03,336 --> 00:28:05,097
-I got some news about Graver.

697
00:28:05,131 --> 00:28:07,340
A friend of mine is a trustee
in the jail hospital,

698
00:28:07,375 --> 00:28:08,963
and he tipped me off
they're moving Graver out

699
00:28:08,997 --> 00:28:10,205
and in an ambulance
this afternoon.

700
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:11,310
-My trusty friend.

701
00:28:11,344 --> 00:28:12,311
-Is there anything
we can do about it?

702
00:28:12,345 --> 00:28:14,175
-Yeah. I got it all figured out.

703
00:28:14,209 --> 00:28:17,109
Now, my friend told me which
road the ambulance is taking.

704
00:28:17,143 --> 00:28:19,974
-[Mumbling]

705
00:28:20,008 --> 00:28:21,113
♪♪

706
00:28:21,147 --> 00:28:22,631
-Lay down.

707
00:28:22,666 --> 00:28:25,013
-What a party.

708
00:28:25,048 --> 00:28:27,671
I was so hammered.

709
00:28:27,706 --> 00:28:29,155
♪♪

710
00:28:29,190 --> 00:28:32,641
[Tires screech]

711
00:28:32,676 --> 00:28:35,161
-Look, guys. It's roadkill.

712
00:28:35,196 --> 00:28:38,164
♪♪

713
00:28:38,199 --> 00:28:39,994
-Huh?

714
00:28:40,028 --> 00:28:41,202
-All right.

715
00:28:41,236 --> 00:28:42,824
Give me a snow cone
and two Bomb Pops.

716
00:28:42,859 --> 00:28:45,551
-Start walking, cross-country.

717
00:28:45,585 --> 00:28:47,691
Go on!
-I'm wearing white, though!

718
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:50,521
That's not very good humor.

719
00:28:50,556 --> 00:28:51,833
Geez.

720
00:28:51,868 --> 00:28:59,358
♪♪

721
00:28:59,392 --> 00:29:01,774
-That's got to hurt.

722
00:29:01,809 --> 00:29:04,294
-What about the driver?

723
00:29:04,328 --> 00:29:06,434
-I sent him hiking.
-You should've slugged him.

724
00:29:06,468 --> 00:29:07,469
As soon as he gets to a phone,

725
00:29:07,504 --> 00:29:08,470
he'll have the cops
on our trail.

726
00:29:08,505 --> 00:29:09,886
-Oh, that's okay.

727
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:11,784
There's a car parked a few milesup the road to pick you up.

728
00:29:11,819 --> 00:29:13,786
-Okay, let's go.

729
00:29:13,821 --> 00:29:18,308
-Wow, now they can have all the
frozen treats they ever wanted!

730
00:29:18,342 --> 00:29:20,137
-That's a haul.

731
00:29:20,172 --> 00:29:24,970
♪♪

732
00:29:25,004 --> 00:29:26,385
Cool car.

733
00:29:26,419 --> 00:29:28,697
That's a cool Cody Car.

734
00:29:28,732 --> 00:29:32,874
♪♪

735
00:29:32,909 --> 00:29:34,669
-Hey, wait a minute.

736
00:29:34,703 --> 00:29:36,671
There's no ice cream
on these sticks!

737
00:29:36,705 --> 00:29:40,088
-Those are tongue depressors.This is an ambulance, you idiot!

738
00:29:40,123 --> 00:29:41,158
-Oh!

739
00:29:41,193 --> 00:29:44,472
-It's about time you got here.

740
00:29:44,506 --> 00:29:45,714
The cops are after you already.

741
00:29:45,749 --> 00:29:47,130
-Oh, no.
-What?

742
00:29:47,164 --> 00:29:48,994
-Yeah, it's coming over
the radio right now.

743
00:29:49,028 --> 00:29:50,996
-But check local listings
in your area.

744
00:29:51,030 --> 00:29:53,136
♪♪

745
00:29:53,170 --> 00:29:55,552
-Calling all cars.
Calling all cars.

746
00:29:55,586 --> 00:29:57,312
The stolen ambulance
was last reported

747
00:29:57,347 --> 00:30:00,005
turning onto the east end
of Harrison Canyon Highway.

748
00:30:00,039 --> 00:30:02,214
-I told you you should've
slugged that driver.

749
00:30:02,248 --> 00:30:04,078
-Calling police headquarters.

750
00:30:04,112 --> 00:30:06,045
Calling police headquarters.

751
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:08,876
-It's Cody.
-Police headquarters, come in.

752
00:30:08,910 --> 00:30:10,084
-This is Commando Cody.

753
00:30:10,118 --> 00:30:11,568
I picked up your broadcast,

754
00:30:11,602 --> 00:30:13,708
and I'm just turning into thewest end of Harrison Canyon now.

755
00:30:13,742 --> 00:30:14,916
-Think that's an honorary title?

756
00:30:14,951 --> 00:30:17,056
-Meet the ambulance.
I'll stop it for you.

757
00:30:17,091 --> 00:30:19,196
-We'll get some men up there
soon as we can.

758
00:30:19,231 --> 00:30:21,716
-That's a bad break.
What's he doing out here?

759
00:30:21,750 --> 00:30:23,822
-Probably on his way
to third-degree me.

760
00:30:23,856 --> 00:30:25,513
I'll go back to town with you,
Sam.

761
00:30:25,547 --> 00:30:26,583
You keep going
with the ambulance

762
00:30:26,617 --> 00:30:27,653
until you can ditch it.

763
00:30:27,687 --> 00:30:29,517
If you meet Cody first,
smash him.

764
00:30:29,551 --> 00:30:30,656
-Right.

765
00:30:30,690 --> 00:30:32,209
-Man, he should just
get some counseling.

766
00:30:32,244 --> 00:30:34,556
He wouldn't want to smash peopleall the time.

767
00:30:34,591 --> 00:30:38,077
-Smash, slug, shoot, walk --
it's all the same to him.

768
00:30:38,112 --> 00:30:40,183
He just wasn't beat up enough
as a kid.

769
00:30:40,217 --> 00:30:47,224
♪♪

770
00:30:47,259 --> 00:30:48,536
-We now return you

771
00:30:48,570 --> 00:30:53,230
to the All Car Chase Network
already in progress.

772
00:30:53,265 --> 00:30:55,232
-You think we'll meet them
on the road?

773
00:30:55,267 --> 00:30:56,302
-Well,
if I read my script right,

774
00:30:56,337 --> 00:30:59,892
we should be meeting them
pretty soon.

775
00:30:59,927 --> 00:31:03,240
-I ever tell you guys about
how James Dean died?

776
00:31:03,275 --> 00:31:13,250
♪♪

777
00:31:13,285 --> 00:31:20,706
♪♪

778
00:31:20,740 --> 00:31:23,536
-What'd I tell you?
There he is, page 92.

779
00:31:23,571 --> 00:31:26,539
♪♪

780
00:31:26,574 --> 00:31:27,989
-There it is.

781
00:31:28,024 --> 00:31:31,717
♪♪

782
00:31:31,751 --> 00:31:33,098
It's going to crash into us!

783
00:31:33,132 --> 00:31:36,377
-Nah, we've done this
a million times!

784
00:31:36,411 --> 00:31:38,379
-Oh.-Ooh, we got to get out of here.

785
00:31:38,413 --> 00:31:45,489
