♪♪

1036
00:42:25,612 --> 00:42:27,683
-Cool.

1037
00:42:27,717 --> 00:42:30,030
-Hmm, Estes model rockets.

1038
00:42:30,064 --> 00:42:32,377
♪♪

1039
00:42:32,411 --> 00:42:34,586
-Comes from a planet
where they evolved from apes

1040
00:42:34,621 --> 00:42:36,243
and water coolers.

1041
00:42:36,277 --> 00:42:38,521
-Home planet,
stop my milk delivery.

1042
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:39,867
Pick up my mail.

1043
00:42:39,902 --> 00:42:44,078
-Extension Ro-Man X-J-2
reporting to Guidance Ro-Man.

1044
00:42:44,113 --> 00:42:45,355
I salute you.

1045
00:42:45,390 --> 00:42:47,357
-You are late 14 minutes.

1046
00:42:47,392 --> 00:42:48,600
-The lights were against me.

1047
00:42:48,635 --> 00:42:50,740
-Gravitational pull
is stronger than reported,

1048
00:42:50,775 --> 00:42:53,640
0.7652 higher than our planet.

1049
00:42:53,674 --> 00:42:56,021
-Accepted. Report.

1050
00:42:56,056 --> 00:42:57,022
-He is so gullible.

1051
00:42:57,057 --> 00:42:59,300
-May I ask first for other news?

1052
00:42:59,335 --> 00:43:00,612
-Granted.

1053
00:43:00,647 --> 00:43:03,063
No life has been discovered
on any other planets.

1054
00:43:03,097 --> 00:43:05,030
Earth is our only rival.

1055
00:43:05,065 --> 00:43:06,998
-Was, Great Guidance.
-What's he looking through?

1056
00:43:07,032 --> 00:43:08,344
-A glass darkly.

1057
00:43:08,378 --> 00:43:10,795
-...energy had not mastered
the cosmic ray.

1058
00:43:10,829 --> 00:43:14,281
Wherever I directed the
calcinator beam, they crumbled.

1059
00:43:14,315 --> 00:43:16,179
At first, the fools
thought it came from

1060
00:43:16,214 --> 00:43:17,974
one among their many nations.

1061
00:43:18,009 --> 00:43:22,669
They began destroying each otherwith hydrogen bombs.

1062
00:43:22,703 --> 00:43:25,672
I announced myself to keep them
from wiping out cities,

1063
00:43:25,706 --> 00:43:28,088
which will give our people
much amusement.

1064
00:43:28,122 --> 00:43:30,538
-Oh, good, you saved Six Flags
and Disneyland, great.

1065
00:43:30,573 --> 00:43:32,644
-Too late
they banded against me.

1066
00:43:32,679 --> 00:43:34,646
Their resistance pattern
showed some intelligence.

1067
00:43:34,681 --> 00:43:36,544
-Is he looking into a mirror?
-But all are gone now.

1068
00:43:36,579 --> 00:43:37,856
-It's like
he's a schizophrenic ape.

1069
00:43:37,891 --> 00:43:39,340
-The way is clear
for our people.

1070
00:43:39,375 --> 00:43:41,480
-He's got problems.
-I want facts, not words.

1071
00:43:41,515 --> 00:43:42,827
-Yeah.

1072
00:43:42,861 --> 00:43:47,417
-Fact A -- My pulse has been
reduced to plus zero zero.

1073
00:43:47,452 --> 00:43:48,695
-Reject.

1074
00:43:48,729 --> 00:43:51,629
Pair off.
-Pair...

1075
00:43:51,663 --> 00:43:53,734
But, Great Guidance,
I approved it.

1076
00:43:53,769 --> 00:43:56,564
My energizer has scan-checked
by square feet.

1077
00:43:56,599 --> 00:43:59,188
No life
above Lepidoptera level exists.

1078
00:43:59,222 --> 00:44:01,155
-My computator is more accurate.

1079
00:44:01,190 --> 00:44:02,605
-Got a monkey on his back.

1080
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:05,608
-In the 22nd category, there is
an error of 16 billionths.

1081
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:07,783
-Great One is never wrong.

1082
00:44:07,817 --> 00:44:10,924
Then there are perhaps
eight people left on Earth?

1083
00:44:10,958 --> 00:44:13,651
-Not perhaps, precisely.

1084
00:44:13,685 --> 00:44:16,757
Find and destroy them,
then report back.

1085
00:44:16,792 --> 00:44:24,972
♪♪

1086
00:44:26,698 --> 00:44:28,631
-It's the Berlin Wall.
-No, it's --

1087
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:29,701
This is the future.

1088
00:44:29,736 --> 00:44:31,530
That's the Great Wall
of Cleveland.

1089
00:44:31,565 --> 00:44:32,704
-Oh.

1090
00:44:32,739 --> 00:44:34,706
-I don't think that wiring
was up to code.

1091
00:44:34,741 --> 00:44:38,330
[Electricity crackling]

1092
00:44:38,365 --> 00:44:39,538
-Hey.

1093
00:44:39,573 --> 00:44:42,127
They get the stuff?

1094
00:44:46,580 --> 00:44:50,170
-Come on in.

1095
00:44:50,204 --> 00:44:52,034
-He's got to build a step
sometime.

1096
00:44:52,068 --> 00:44:54,174
-Pa, what do you think?

1097
00:44:54,208 --> 00:44:56,348
-I have a good mind
to give you a thrashing.

1098
00:44:56,383 --> 00:44:58,765
Didn't we tell you never,
never, never to go outside

1099
00:44:58,799 --> 00:45:01,077
of those wires
without our permission?

1100
00:45:01,112 --> 00:45:05,254
-Mother, anger won't keep
the boy from doing it again.

1101
00:45:05,288 --> 00:45:08,188
You must tell him why.

1102
00:45:08,222 --> 00:45:10,811
You know the terrible things
that have happened

1103
00:45:10,846 --> 00:45:13,089
when the Ro-Man landed on Earth.

1104
00:45:13,124 --> 00:45:15,160
The only reason
we are still alive

1105
00:45:15,195 --> 00:45:17,576
is that your sister, Alice,
and I

1106
00:45:17,611 --> 00:45:20,856
worked out a way to reflect
his deadly beams...

1107
00:45:20,890 --> 00:45:22,789
-Oh.
-...away from the house.

1108
00:45:22,823 --> 00:45:24,342
He can't see us.

1109
00:45:24,376 --> 00:45:28,622
He can't hear us, but one word
spoken outside the barrier,

1110
00:45:28,656 --> 00:45:30,210
and he will be down on us.

1111
00:45:30,244 --> 00:45:31,349
-Like ugly on an ape.

1112
00:45:31,383 --> 00:45:32,695
-Do you understand that, Johnny?

1113
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:35,180
-But I saw him.
-Saw who?

1114
00:45:35,215 --> 00:45:38,149
-Ro-Man -- he's in the cave
at the end of the ravine.

1115
00:45:38,183 --> 00:45:39,322
-Then he's found us out.

1116
00:45:39,357 --> 00:45:40,668
-Not yet,
or we'd all by dead by now.

1117
00:45:40,703 --> 00:45:41,980
Are you sure?
-We'd be crispy fritters.

1118
00:45:42,015 --> 00:45:43,844
-I was in the cave
painting these pictures

1119
00:45:43,879 --> 00:45:45,639
the way we saw him
on the viewer screen.

1120
00:45:45,673 --> 00:45:47,089
-Why were you doing that,
Johnny?

1121
00:45:47,123 --> 00:45:49,229
-So in case he did wipe out
the human race,

1122
00:45:49,263 --> 00:45:51,024
there'd be some record
of how it happened.

1123
00:45:51,058 --> 00:45:52,404
-Go on. Go on.

1124
00:45:52,439 --> 00:45:54,199
-Johnny, don't be a hero.
Don't be a fool with your life.

1125
00:45:54,234 --> 00:45:55,511
-...ducked out just in time.

1126
00:45:55,545 --> 00:45:57,547
Looked to me like
he was making it his home.

1127
00:45:57,582 --> 00:45:58,721
-Why here?

1128
00:45:58,756 --> 00:46:00,412
Why so close?
-It's near the mall.

1129
00:46:00,447 --> 00:46:02,138
-Maybe we could kill him, Papa.

1130
00:46:02,173 --> 00:46:05,314
-No, Johnny, the armies
of the entire world

1131
00:46:05,348 --> 00:46:07,212
tried and failed.

1132
00:46:07,247 --> 00:46:11,423
We have thrown everything we hadat him, but he's impervious.

1133
00:46:11,458 --> 00:46:13,840
-Unless we can find
his weak spot.

1134
00:46:13,874 --> 00:46:16,981
-Like his underwear line?
-Ew.

1135
00:46:17,015 --> 00:46:18,499
-Yes, dear.
-We have all the bananas.

1136
00:46:18,534 --> 00:46:19,707
-Why here?
-We have all the power.

1137
00:46:19,742 --> 00:46:21,675
-Why here?

1138
00:46:21,709 --> 00:46:24,160
[Electricity crackling]

1139
00:46:24,195 --> 00:46:26,818
-Perhaps we're the last people
on Earth, Dad.

1140
00:46:26,853 --> 00:46:32,134
He senses our presence and keepscalculating closer and closer.

1141
00:46:32,168 --> 00:46:33,998
-I don't believe that.

1142
00:46:34,032 --> 00:46:37,070
I'm sure there were
some other scientific minds

1143
00:46:37,104 --> 00:46:40,694
capable of rigging a foil
to prevent detection.

1144
00:46:40,728 --> 00:46:43,835
-With even worse accents.
-If we only could find the way,

1145
00:46:43,870 --> 00:46:47,839
only one way of communication
with each other.

1146
00:46:47,874 --> 00:46:50,877
-Do you think we still have a
garrison on the space platform?

1147
00:46:50,911 --> 00:46:53,534
Ro-Man hasn't
destroyed that yet.

1148
00:46:53,569 --> 00:46:55,847
-Well...

1149
00:46:55,882 --> 00:46:58,401
it could be.

1150
00:46:58,436 --> 00:47:02,026
If we only could
get through to them,

1151
00:47:02,060 --> 00:47:04,856
but why should we succeed
where others failed?

1152
00:47:04,891 --> 00:47:06,789
-Don't you talk like that, dear.

1153
00:47:06,824 --> 00:47:09,136
-I have to talk like that.
I'm German.

1154
00:47:09,171 --> 00:47:10,758
[High-pitched whining]

1155
00:47:10,793 --> 00:47:13,865
-Excuse me.
-Hey, the cookies are done.

1156
00:47:13,900 --> 00:47:15,729
-This may be them.

1157
00:47:15,763 --> 00:47:18,594
Maybe they are coming through
from the space platform.

1158
00:47:22,011 --> 00:47:24,565
-Humans, listen to me.

1159
00:47:24,600 --> 00:47:26,360
-Okay.

1160
00:47:26,395 --> 00:47:28,017
-Due to an error in calculation,

1161
00:47:28,052 --> 00:47:29,674
there are still
a few of you left.

1162
00:47:29,708 --> 00:47:31,193
-We sincerely apologize

1163
00:47:31,227 --> 00:47:33,885
for any inconvenience
it may have caused you.

1164
00:47:33,920 --> 00:47:35,887
-Now I know you are watching.

1165
00:47:35,922 --> 00:47:39,063
I see five of you
who have not been destroyed.

1166
00:47:39,097 --> 00:47:42,514
Show yourselves, and I promise
you a painless death.

1167
00:47:42,549 --> 00:47:44,344
-Uh, we're looking at
a few other offers first.

1168
00:47:44,378 --> 00:47:48,279
-Just the five of us left?
But this is incredible.

1169
00:47:48,313 --> 00:47:50,868
It means that Roy is gone, too.

1170
00:47:50,902 --> 00:47:52,352
-I'll bet Alice is happy,

1171
00:47:52,386 --> 00:47:54,354
the way they used to fight.
-Hey.

1172
00:47:54,388 --> 00:47:56,528
-Don't say that, Johnny.
-Don't ever say that.

1173
00:47:56,563 --> 00:47:58,185
-Roy was a great scientist.

1174
00:47:58,220 --> 00:48:01,119
-I would have never developed
the serum without him.

1175
00:48:01,154 --> 00:48:02,845
-Maple serum?
-The trouble was he --

1176
00:48:02,880 --> 00:48:05,641
he wouldn't admit
I was good in my field.

1177
00:48:05,675 --> 00:48:07,401
-Anyone who could fix
that view screen

1178
00:48:07,436 --> 00:48:10,646
after what that blast did to it
is better than good.

1179
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:13,787
-Hmm, easy, easy.

1180
00:48:13,821 --> 00:48:16,065
-I'm sorry.

1181
00:48:16,100 --> 00:48:18,309
Seems silly after
all the terrible things that

1182
00:48:18,343 --> 00:48:23,072
have happened to go to pieces
over one miserable,

1183
00:48:23,107 --> 00:48:26,524
egotistical, impossible guy.

1184
00:48:26,558 --> 00:48:29,320
-Goodness, I love him.
-Oh, Roy.

1185
00:48:29,354 --> 00:48:33,427
-Sure, he's a jerk,
but he's my jerk.

1186
00:48:33,462 --> 00:48:35,982
-Do you wonder what happened
to your fellows?

1187
00:48:36,016 --> 00:48:37,328
-Yeah.
-Watch them.

1188
00:48:37,362 --> 00:48:39,640
-They were forced to watch
boring war documentaries.

1189
00:48:39,675 --> 00:48:42,333
-Hey, my fellows
never looked like buildings.

1190
00:48:42,367 --> 00:48:44,162
-I'm not watching this.

1191
00:48:44,197 --> 00:48:45,646
♪♪

1192
00:48:45,681 --> 00:48:51,963
[Electricity crackling]

1193
00:48:51,998 --> 00:48:58,452
♪♪

1194
00:48:58,487 --> 00:49:01,559
-Servo, Servo, come in,
my faithful servant.

1195
00:49:01,593 --> 00:49:03,561
-I am here, Your Excellency.

1196
00:49:03,595 --> 00:49:05,459
-Why have not
you killed the human?

1197
00:49:05,494 --> 00:49:07,151
-Because he gives me
crunchy treats,

1198
00:49:07,185 --> 00:49:08,669
and he empties my load pan.

1199
00:49:08,704 --> 00:49:10,982
-But he is human
and unfit to live.

1200
00:49:11,017 --> 00:49:12,363
-But he's kind of cute.

1201
00:49:12,397 --> 00:49:15,262
He has good bone structure,
and he can drive a stick.

1202
00:49:15,297 --> 00:49:17,471
-There is no room
for your petty sentimentality

1203
00:49:17,506 --> 00:49:19,957
or your -- He can drive a stick?

1204
00:49:19,991 --> 00:49:21,993
Uh, nevertheless, he is human.

1205
00:49:22,028 --> 00:49:25,134
Kill him by sundown,
or you will feel my wrath.

1206
00:49:25,169 --> 00:49:26,377
-Okay. I will try,

1207
00:49:26,411 --> 00:49:28,827
but I do not think
he is going to like it much.

1208
00:49:28,862 --> 00:49:31,313
-You have the effrontery
to defy my orders?

1209
00:49:31,347 --> 00:49:32,797
-Oh, no, nothing like that, sir.

1210
00:49:32,831 --> 00:49:34,523
I'm -- I'm getting a call
on the other line.

1211
00:49:34,557 --> 00:49:35,869
I'm going to have to put you
on hold,

1212
00:49:35,903 --> 00:49:37,112
oh,
Supreme Being of the Universe.

1213
00:49:37,146 --> 00:49:39,010
Oh, rats, I got to
shut this thing off.

1214
00:49:39,045 --> 00:49:40,632
-This is no party line, dolt.

1215
00:49:40,667 --> 00:49:42,841
Try to play telephone tag
with me, you clinkering,

1216
00:49:42,876 --> 00:49:46,500
clankering mishmash of discardedHarley-Davidson remnants.

1217
00:49:46,535 --> 00:49:49,158
Oh, the Earth man
approaches now.

1218
00:49:49,193 --> 00:49:50,263
Destroy him.

1219
00:49:50,297 --> 00:49:51,678
-Oh, I -- I must destroy
the Earth man.

1220
00:49:51,712 --> 00:49:54,474
-Hey, Crow, Tom Servo.
What's up?

1221
00:49:54,508 --> 00:49:56,510
-Your number, I'm afraid.
I must kill you...

1222
00:49:56,545 --> 00:49:57,546
-Huh?
-...Mr. Bond.

1223
00:49:57,580 --> 00:49:58,547
I must kill you now.

1224
00:49:58,581 --> 00:49:59,858
Whoa.

1225
00:49:59,893 --> 00:50:02,654
-Joel, what happened?

1226
00:50:02,689 --> 00:50:04,518
-Uh, Tom Servo is --

1227
00:50:04,553 --> 00:50:06,658
His reason circuits
must have burnt out.

1228
00:50:06,693 --> 00:50:08,039
He tried to kill me.

1229
00:50:08,074 --> 00:50:11,111
-Oh, no, Joel, we were just
doing a little role-playing,

1230
00:50:11,146 --> 00:50:13,734
you know, kill the human
role-play like in the movie.

1231
00:50:13,769 --> 00:50:16,530
-Oh, no, Tom Servo, buddy,
you got to wake up.

1232
00:50:16,565 --> 00:50:19,706
-Ow, my aching chem sphere.
What happened?

1233
00:50:19,740 --> 00:50:21,190
-Man, I'm -- I'm sorry, Tom.

1234
00:50:21,225 --> 00:50:22,881
I didn't know you were kidding.

1235
00:50:22,916 --> 00:50:26,678
-Oh, man, somebody must have
forgotten the robotic laws

1236
00:50:26,713 --> 00:50:28,232
of Isaac Asimov, I think.

1237
00:50:28,266 --> 00:50:29,578
-I'm - I know. I'm sorry.

1238
00:50:29,612 --> 00:50:32,891
A robot can never kill a human.

1239
00:50:32,926 --> 00:50:34,169
-Right.
-I'm really sorry.

1240
00:50:34,203 --> 00:50:36,343
What can I do
to make it up to you, Tom?

1241
00:50:36,378 --> 00:50:37,724
-You could let me kill you,

1242
00:50:37,758 --> 00:50:39,208
Mr. Bond.
-Huh?

1243
00:50:39,243 --> 00:50:40,899
-You could let me --

1244
00:50:40,934 --> 00:50:43,419
Ah, ah!
-He was kidding.

1245
00:50:43,454 --> 00:50:45,732
-Oh, no, we got movie sign!

1246
00:50:45,766 --> 00:50:48,735
[Doors whooshing]

1247
00:50:48,769 --> 00:50:55,914
♪♪

1248
00:50:55,949 --> 00:50:57,916
[Electricity crackling]

1249
00:50:57,951 --> 00:51:00,160
I'm sorry.

1250
00:51:00,195 --> 00:51:01,161
I didn't know
you were you were kidding.

1251
00:51:01,196 --> 00:51:02,231
-Don't ever do that.

1252
00:51:02,266 --> 00:51:03,991
I don't have a breakaway body,
Joel.

1253
00:51:04,026 --> 00:51:05,027
-I thought it was cool.

1254
00:51:05,062 --> 00:51:07,167
-Yeah, of course you did.

1255
00:51:07,202 --> 00:51:09,549
Looks like their futon
survived the holocaust.

1256
00:51:09,583 --> 00:51:11,516
-It's for us.

1257
00:51:11,551 --> 00:51:14,554
[Rumbling]

1258
00:51:14,588 --> 00:51:15,900
-Hi there. Anybody home?

1259
00:51:15,934 --> 00:51:16,970
-It's Roy!
-Oh, he is here.

1260
00:51:17,004 --> 00:51:18,696
-Roy!
-Boy, their survival clothing

1261
00:51:18,730 --> 00:51:21,043
must be getting pretty gamy
by now.

1262
00:51:21,078 --> 00:51:23,045
-Do you know who's in the cave
at the end of the ravine?

1263
00:51:23,080 --> 00:51:24,391
-Ro-Man.
-Ro-Man.

1264
00:51:24,426 --> 00:51:26,669
- Well, uh, I -- I was
as close to him as I am to you.

1265
00:51:26,704 --> 00:51:28,050
-So was I.

1266
00:51:28,085 --> 00:51:29,534
-But he didn't know
that I was there.

1267
00:51:29,569 --> 00:51:30,570
-Do you know why?

1268
00:51:30,604 --> 00:51:31,916
-Maybe you're not
worth noticing.

1269
00:51:31,950 --> 00:51:33,538
-Oh, now I know
I'm in the right house.

1270
00:51:33,573 --> 00:51:38,060
-Yes, and a moment ago, she was
crying because you were dead.

1271
00:51:38,095 --> 00:51:39,682
-You didn't have to waste
any tears on me, honey.

1272
00:51:39,717 --> 00:51:41,098
I bear a charmed life.

1273
00:51:41,132 --> 00:51:42,237
-Except in the shirt department.

1274
00:51:42,271 --> 00:51:44,170
-Ro-Man spoke to us
over the view screen.

1275
00:51:44,204 --> 00:51:47,380
He said that we are the last
five people on the Earth.

1276
00:51:47,414 --> 00:51:50,210
Is he lying,
or are there any other people?

1277
00:51:50,245 --> 00:51:52,454
-Two more, Jason and McCloud.

1278
00:51:52,488 --> 00:51:53,696
-But why them?

1279
00:51:53,731 --> 00:51:55,836
That doesn't make sense.
-Oh, doesn't it?

1280
00:51:55,871 --> 00:51:58,425
Look, the professor here
spends his entire life

1281
00:51:58,460 --> 00:52:01,152
trying to discover a serum,
an antibiotic serum

1282
00:52:01,187 --> 00:52:03,154
that will cure all diseases,
even the common cold, and...

1283
00:52:03,189 --> 00:52:04,811
-We're listening.
-...thanks to his wise choice

1284
00:52:04,845 --> 00:52:07,538
of assistants,
he manages to achieve his goal.

1285
00:52:07,572 --> 00:52:08,780
-Uh-huh.
-And so who does he

1286
00:52:08,815 --> 00:52:10,437
experiment on
with his first injections?

1287
00:52:10,472 --> 00:52:11,783
-Monkeys?

1288
00:52:11,818 --> 00:52:14,890
-Himself, his family, myself,
and Jason and McCloud.

1289
00:52:14,924 --> 00:52:17,030
Therefore, the great antibiotic

1290
00:52:17,064 --> 00:52:19,860
is also the immunizer
to Ro-Man's death ray.

1291
00:52:19,895 --> 00:52:22,346
-And I thought it was
the electronic barricade

1292
00:52:22,380 --> 00:52:23,933
around the house.
-Aw.

1293
00:52:23,968 --> 00:52:26,039
-Well, that may prevent Ro-Man
from finding us

1294
00:52:26,073 --> 00:52:27,696
and blowing us up.
-Which is nothing.

1295
00:52:27,730 --> 00:52:29,870
-But against the sweep of
the death-ray, it's powerless.

1296
00:52:29,905 --> 00:52:31,872
No, the serum, that's the thing.-Chocolate serum?

1297
00:52:31,907 --> 00:52:33,598
-Couldn't you find any more
in the lab?

1298
00:52:33,633 --> 00:52:35,842
-Plenty, but I didn't bring it.

1299
00:52:35,876 --> 00:52:37,119
-Why?
-Hmm?

1300
00:52:37,154 --> 00:52:38,638
-Because we managed
to get together enough fuel

1301
00:52:38,672 --> 00:52:40,571
to take a rocket ship
to the space platform.

1302
00:52:40,605 --> 00:52:41,882
-Smart.
-There's enough serum onboard

1303
00:52:41,917 --> 00:52:43,884
to immunize
the entire garrison there.

1304
00:52:43,919 --> 00:52:45,162
-Apricot serum?
-Does the garrison

1305
00:52:45,196 --> 00:52:46,680
know you're coming?
-Well, how could I tell them

1306
00:52:46,715 --> 00:52:48,199
without
letting Ro-Man know, too?

1307
00:52:48,234 --> 00:52:50,374
-They know
what's going on down here.

1308
00:52:50,408 --> 00:52:51,720
They'll figure it's Ro-Man

1309
00:52:51,754 --> 00:52:53,687
and blast the ship
right out of the sky.

1310
00:52:53,722 --> 00:52:55,620
We'll have to get word
to the space platform.

1311
00:52:55,655 --> 00:52:56,863
That's all.

1312
00:52:56,897 --> 00:52:59,210
-Jason and McCloud take off
in two days.

1313
00:52:59,245 --> 00:53:01,523
On foot, it would take me longerthan that to get back there.

1314
00:53:01,557 --> 00:53:02,903
-Jason, M-McCloud?

1315
00:53:02,938 --> 00:53:04,077
Is Dennis Weaver in this film?

1316
00:53:04,111 --> 00:53:05,458
-...rewire the circuits
on the view screen

1317
00:53:05,492 --> 00:53:07,736
so that we can broadcast
without Ro-Man picking it up.

1318
00:53:07,770 --> 00:53:08,806
-That's it.

1319
00:53:08,840 --> 00:53:11,326
-Such a complicated job
in two days?

1320
00:53:11,360 --> 00:53:14,467
-Well, at least I can try.

1321
00:53:14,501 --> 00:53:17,194
If I only had a decent assistantwho could take orders

1322
00:53:17,228 --> 00:53:19,196
instead of trying
to be the boss.

1323
00:53:19,230 --> 00:53:20,611
-I'm bossy? You're so bossy,

1324
00:53:20,645 --> 00:53:22,509
you ought to be milked
before you come home at night.

1325
00:53:22,544 --> 00:53:23,855
-Dibs.
-I'll -- I'll do that.

1326
00:53:23,890 --> 00:53:25,202
-I'll get a stool and a pail.
-All right.

1327
00:53:25,236 --> 00:53:27,204
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
-That's udder-ly ridiculous.

1328
00:53:27,238 --> 00:53:28,688
-Oh, cow could you say that?

1329
00:53:28,722 --> 00:53:30,862
-Are you going to milk this
for all it's worth?

1330
00:53:30,897 --> 00:53:33,071
♪♪

1331
00:53:33,106 --> 00:53:34,349
-Don't you have to loop it?

1332
00:53:34,383 --> 00:53:36,040
-Roy, will you not argue,
please?

1333
00:53:36,074 --> 00:53:38,525
-Looks like
a steam-powered soldering iron.

1334
00:53:38,560 --> 00:53:40,113
-You're either too beautiful
to be so smart

1335
00:53:40,147 --> 00:53:43,220
or too smart to be so beautiful.

1336
00:53:43,254 --> 00:53:45,567
-I guess we do get along
all right at that,

1337
00:53:45,601 --> 00:53:48,846
but let's work together now
and we can play later.

1338
00:53:48,880 --> 00:53:51,711
-Some people really have
a strange idea about foreplay.

1339
00:53:51,745 --> 00:53:53,368
-Roy, oh, what time is it?

1340
00:53:53,402 --> 00:53:54,852
-It's Miller time.
-4:30.

1341
00:53:54,886 --> 00:53:56,233
-And what day, Roy? I can't...

1342
00:53:56,267 --> 00:53:58,235
-It's Miller day.

1343
00:53:58,269 --> 00:54:00,237
-I'm so tired.

1344
00:54:00,271 --> 00:54:02,480
♪♪

1345
00:54:02,515 --> 00:54:06,001
There, there.

1346
00:54:06,035 --> 00:54:08,659
-Ouch, ouch, hot.
-Oh, Roy, we'll never make it.

1347
00:54:08,693 --> 00:54:10,488
-Hot.

1348
00:54:10,523 --> 00:54:12,490
♪♪

1349
00:54:12,525 --> 00:54:14,665
-I can't control my hands
anymore.

1350
00:54:14,699 --> 00:54:16,874
-Let's rest a little.
-Oh, but we can't.

1351
00:54:16,908 --> 00:54:18,013
-Roy is right.

1352
00:54:18,047 --> 00:54:20,671
It's time you get some sleep,
Alice.

1353
00:54:20,705 --> 00:54:23,329
-Jiminy,
two days you've been at it.

1354
00:54:23,363 --> 00:54:25,676
-Oh, not that long.
It can't be that long.

1355
00:54:25,710 --> 00:54:26,884
-It is.

1356
00:54:26,918 --> 00:54:28,541
-The rocket ship
must have taken off at dawn.

1357
00:54:28,575 --> 00:54:30,336
They're either there by now...

1358
00:54:30,370 --> 00:54:32,338
-Two darks, two lights,
that's two days, right?

1359
00:54:32,372 --> 00:54:33,684
-I'm sorry, Dad.
-Failed?

1360
00:54:33,718 --> 00:54:35,651
Do you realize that what
you tried to was impossible,

1361
00:54:35,686 --> 00:54:36,859
yet you almost did it?

1362
00:54:36,894 --> 00:54:40,069
-But I didn't.
-That's why it's impossible.

1363
00:54:40,104 --> 00:54:42,555
-Now, this is what Dr. Corneliuswould look like

1364
00:54:42,589 --> 00:54:44,867
if he was played
by Raymond Burr.

1365
00:54:44,902 --> 00:54:49,216
♪♪

1366
00:54:49,251 --> 00:54:51,218
-You know, you'd think if
he was going to rule the world,

1367
00:54:51,253 --> 00:54:53,531
he'd pick a better spot
than a cave.

1368
00:54:53,566 --> 00:54:55,602
-It's got a bus line.

1369
00:54:55,637 --> 00:54:58,571
-And it's, uh, rent-controlled.

1370
00:54:58,605 --> 00:55:01,815
-Time for another fireside chat
with Ro-Man.

1371
00:55:01,850 --> 00:55:04,162
-Now I find six.

1372
00:55:04,197 --> 00:55:06,337
-He still doesn't know about
Jason and McCloud.

1373
00:55:06,372 --> 00:55:07,580
-Yeah, but you just told him.

1374
00:55:07,614 --> 00:55:09,064
-There were eight of you.

1375
00:55:09,098 --> 00:55:11,825
The Guidance Ro-Man who
understands everything

1376
00:55:11,860 --> 00:55:13,137
showed me that.

1377
00:55:13,171 --> 00:55:15,484
Yet I might have had trouble
locating the other two

1378
00:55:15,519 --> 00:55:17,106
had they not taken off
in a rocket ship

1379
00:55:17,141 --> 00:55:19,246
and revealed their presence.

1380
00:55:19,281 --> 00:55:21,835
Look, humans.

1381
00:55:21,870 --> 00:55:23,492
-Hmm?

1382
00:55:23,527 --> 00:55:26,323
-Oh, it's just a V-2 rocket.

1383
00:55:26,357 --> 00:55:29,153
-Aw, he could've had a V-8.

1384
00:55:30,396 --> 00:55:33,191
Joke, Joel, joke.

1385
00:55:33,226 --> 00:55:34,779
Sorry.

1386
00:55:34,814 --> 00:55:35,884
-I thought it was hilarious.

1387
00:55:35,918 --> 00:55:38,058
-They are headed
for the space platform,

1388
00:55:38,093 --> 00:55:40,509
which Guidance Ro-Man spared
because it would have been

1389
00:55:40,544 --> 00:55:46,826
a convenience for my people
when they arrive on Earth.

1390
00:55:46,860 --> 00:55:48,379
-[Laughs] Look at that.

1391
00:55:48,414 --> 00:55:50,519
It's hand-powered.
-The space platform.

1392
00:55:50,554 --> 00:55:52,590
♪♪

1393
00:55:52,625 --> 00:55:55,731
-But now we shall
destroy that, too.

1394
00:55:55,766 --> 00:56:04,015
♪♪

1395
00:56:04,050 --> 00:56:05,603
Alert!

1396
00:56:05,638 --> 00:56:07,847
10, 9, 8...

1397
00:56:07,881 --> 00:56:13,128
-8, 7, 6, 5, 4...

1398
00:56:13,162 --> 00:56:14,474
Hey.
Stay true to your countdown.

1399
00:56:14,509 --> 00:56:16,338
[Electricity crackles]

1400
00:56:16,373 --> 00:56:18,651
-The space platform.

1401
00:56:18,685 --> 00:56:20,377
-The guy could just drop it.

1402
00:56:20,411 --> 00:56:24,001
-That's a Lucas effect,
isn't it?

1403
00:56:24,035 --> 00:56:25,416
-Buddy Lucas.

1404
00:56:25,451 --> 00:56:27,418
-I just saw the hand.

1405
00:56:27,453 --> 00:56:30,041
-Human seven and eight, all.

1406
00:56:30,076 --> 00:56:33,838
-They look really bored.
He should open with a joke.

1407
00:56:33,873 --> 00:56:34,943
-Yeah.

1408
00:56:34,977 --> 00:56:37,186
-...of the two billion,
there are six.

1409
00:56:37,221 --> 00:56:39,844
♪♪

1410
00:56:39,879 --> 00:56:46,368
Calculate your chances --
negative, negative, negative.

1411
00:56:46,403 --> 00:56:48,957
-He's so negative.
-Is there a choice

1412
00:56:48,991 --> 00:56:51,200
between a painless
surrender death

1413
00:56:51,235 --> 00:56:53,202
and the horror
of resistance death?

1414
00:56:53,237 --> 00:56:56,447
-Oh, I didn't know
the death ray had two settings.

1415
00:56:56,482 --> 00:56:59,968
-By your clock time,
in one hour, I seek you out.

1416
00:57:00,002 --> 00:57:02,729
♪♪

1417
00:57:02,764 --> 00:57:04,524
Last warning.

1418
00:57:04,559 --> 00:57:09,287
♪♪

1419
00:57:10,979 --> 00:57:14,154
-The screen turned back
into a refrigerator.

1420
00:57:14,189 --> 00:57:16,812
-Mommy,
why doesn't he like people?

1421
00:57:16,847 --> 00:57:19,332
-He likes most people.
It's just you he hates.

1422
00:57:19,366 --> 00:57:21,507
-I don't know, darling.
-He's not alone.

1423
00:57:21,541 --> 00:57:23,440
-Perhaps if we could
talk to him.

1424
00:57:25,511 --> 00:57:27,547
You better go and rest, too.

1425
00:57:27,582 --> 00:57:28,997
-They just got up.

1426
00:57:29,031 --> 00:57:31,689
-George, we can't go on this waymuch longer.

1427
00:57:31,724 --> 00:57:33,484
Our food is almost gone.

1428
00:57:33,519 --> 00:57:34,865
-What else can we do?

1429
00:57:34,899 --> 00:57:37,350
Commit suicide
or give into Ro-Man...

1430
00:57:37,384 --> 00:57:38,489
-What was the first one again?

1431
00:57:38,524 --> 00:57:40,008
-...as the last people on Earth?

1432
00:57:40,042 --> 00:57:41,803
-George, talk to him.

1433
00:57:41,837 --> 00:57:43,805
They can see
that we won't harm him.

1434
00:57:43,839 --> 00:57:45,634
He can let us live.

1435
00:57:45,669 --> 00:57:48,534
If Alice could've finished
rewiring the view screen,

1436
00:57:48,568 --> 00:57:49,845
you could've talked
to the platform

1437
00:57:49,880 --> 00:57:51,847
without Ro-Man
discovering our presence.

1438
00:57:51,882 --> 00:57:52,917
-But she didn't.

1439
00:57:52,952 --> 00:57:54,022
-Why can't you talk
directly to him?

1440
00:57:54,056 --> 00:57:56,680
-I could. Of course I could.

1441
00:57:56,714 --> 00:58:00,200
As soon as Alice
has had her sleep, I will.

1442
00:58:00,235 --> 00:58:02,513
♪♪

1443
00:58:02,548 --> 00:58:04,964
-What is this,
a Shedd's Spread commercial?

1444
00:58:04,998 --> 00:58:06,517
-Not like that.

1445
00:58:06,552 --> 00:58:07,863
-Alice, look.

1446
00:58:07,898 --> 00:58:10,797
You simply can't connect
these two circuits.

1447
00:58:10,832 --> 00:58:12,937
-Here, let me.

1448
00:58:12,972 --> 00:58:15,561
-Her hands are solderly soft.

1449
00:58:15,595 --> 00:58:18,184
-Hey, Ro-Man got a CD player.

1450
00:58:18,218 --> 00:58:19,841
-And I think
there's a ham radio.

1451
00:58:19,875 --> 00:58:21,325
-And a lunch box.

1452
00:58:21,359 --> 00:58:23,327
-Maybe it's
a ham-and-cheese radio.

1453
00:58:23,361 --> 00:58:25,640
[Chuckles] Ho-ho!
Ham and cheese.

1454
00:58:25,674 --> 00:58:28,194
-He looks like Gino Vannelli
with a kettle head.

1455
00:58:28,228 --> 00:58:33,440
♪♪

1456
00:58:33,475 --> 00:58:35,926
[High-pitched whining]

1457
00:58:35,960 --> 00:58:38,687
-I thought I told you
to never call me here.

1458
00:58:38,722 --> 00:58:44,521
-Ro-Man, Ro-Man, do you scan us
on your view screen?

1459
00:58:44,555 --> 00:58:47,385
-Yes, Earth man, I see you.

1460
00:58:47,420 --> 00:58:49,215
This means only one thing --

1461
00:58:49,249 --> 00:58:51,942
You have decided to take
the easy way out.

1462
00:58:51,976 --> 00:58:55,601
-No, Ro-Man, we have fought you
to a standstill,

1463
00:58:55,635 --> 00:58:59,570
and we will go on doing it
as long as necessary.

1464
00:58:59,605 --> 00:59:02,331
If you try to figure out
our position,

1465
00:59:02,366 --> 00:59:04,368
you are wasting your time.

1466
00:59:04,402 --> 00:59:06,577
-None shall escape me.

1467
00:59:06,612 --> 00:59:11,824
I shall find a way to rid
this Earth planet of humans.

1468
00:59:11,858 --> 00:59:14,274
-No!

1469
00:59:14,309 --> 00:59:17,968
We humans will not give up
this earth of ours.

1470
00:59:18,002 --> 00:59:19,038
-Ever.

1471
00:59:19,072 --> 00:59:21,109
-But let me ask you
something else.

1472
00:59:21,143 --> 00:59:23,594
-Have you thought about your
future, your insurance needs?

1473
00:59:23,629 --> 00:59:28,150
-What do you have to need
from us?

1474
00:59:28,185 --> 00:59:32,016
Let me show you the sick people
you want to destroy.

1475
00:59:32,051 --> 00:59:33,604
-Thanks!
We've been dying to meet them.

1476
00:59:33,639 --> 00:59:36,503
-First, my wife, Martha.

1477
00:59:36,538 --> 00:59:37,919
My companion for 23 years.

1478
00:59:37,953 --> 00:59:40,128
-She bakes a strudel that will
make your pelt stand on end.

1479
00:59:40,162 --> 00:59:43,131
-Is there anything to fear
from this woman?

1480
00:59:43,165 --> 00:59:46,513
-A human woman
is the bringer of human life.

1481
00:59:46,548 --> 00:59:49,309
There must be an end
to your race.

1482
00:59:49,344 --> 00:59:52,899
-Or my children, Alice...

1483
00:59:52,934 --> 00:59:54,004
-No!

1484
00:59:54,038 --> 00:59:56,454
I have a mission to perform.

1485
00:59:56,489 --> 00:59:58,491
-...Carla...
-She can take a nothing day

1486
00:59:58,525 --> 01:00:00,044
and suddenly make it all
seem worth --

1487
01:00:00,079 --> 01:00:02,253
Uh, well, maybe not.

1488
01:00:02,288 --> 01:00:04,014
-...and Johnny.

1489
01:00:04,048 --> 01:00:05,532
-Pbht!

1490
01:00:05,567 --> 01:00:07,638
-The boy is impertinent.

1491
01:00:07,673 --> 01:00:11,573
-Or is it in the etiquette code
of your people

1492
01:00:11,608 --> 01:00:14,093
that children must be murdered?

1493
01:00:14,127 --> 01:00:16,336
-You are not like my people.

1494
01:00:16,371 --> 01:00:18,545
You are savage barbarians.

1495
01:00:18,580 --> 01:00:19,926
Non-Ro-Man.

1496
01:00:19,961 --> 01:00:21,445
Animals!

1497
01:00:21,479 --> 01:00:23,723
-Take my assistant, Roy.
-Please!

1498
01:00:23,758 --> 01:00:26,415
-Who has developed
a serum with me,

1499
01:00:26,450 --> 01:00:30,247
which would have wiped out
disease among my people.

1500
01:00:30,281 --> 01:00:32,042
-Wait!

1501
01:00:32,076 --> 01:00:34,113
-What's my line again?

1502
01:00:34,147 --> 01:00:35,735
Oh, yeah, there is something.
Yeah.

1503
01:00:35,770 --> 01:00:38,117
-There is something
I do not understand quite.

1504
01:00:38,151 --> 01:00:41,223
But I want to see the girl,
Alice, again.

1505
01:00:41,258 --> 01:00:42,673
-Okay, now tilt the camera down
a little.

1506
01:00:42,708 --> 01:00:44,468
-We want peace, Ro-Man.

1507
01:00:44,502 --> 01:00:47,229
But peace with honor.

1508
01:00:47,264 --> 01:00:48,955
-I will talk with the girl.

1509
01:00:48,990 --> 01:00:52,338
It is not in the plan,but although I cannot verify it,

1510
01:00:52,372 --> 01:00:54,512
I feel that she will understand.

1511
01:00:54,547 --> 01:00:56,583
-No!

1512
01:00:56,618 --> 01:00:59,138
I am the head
of this family unit.

1513
01:00:59,172 --> 01:01:00,967
You have to talk with me!

1514
01:01:01,002 --> 01:01:02,693
-Calculate, human.

1515
01:01:02,728 --> 01:01:04,315
If I meet with the girl,

1516
01:01:04,350 --> 01:01:07,560
I may find a way
to integrate you into the plan.

1517
01:01:07,594 --> 01:01:11,702
It is not a fact,
but what you would call a hope.

1518
01:01:11,737 --> 01:01:13,324
-Name the place, Ro-Man.

1519
01:01:13,359 --> 01:01:15,016
I will be there.

1520
01:01:15,050 --> 01:01:16,534
-I do not understand,

1521
01:01:16,569 --> 01:01:20,262
but it is only the onecalled Alice that I want to see.

1522
01:01:20,297 --> 01:01:22,540
-And for some reason,I feel like calling you Dad now.

1523
01:01:22,575 --> 01:01:24,473
-Here I am, Ro-Man.
Where shall we meet?

1524
01:01:24,508 --> 01:01:26,683
-Behind the junior high school
gym, right after math.

1525
01:01:26,717 --> 01:01:29,858
-...dry rivers,
there is a ruin there.

1526
01:01:29,893 --> 01:01:31,653
I will meet you in an hour.

1527
01:01:31,688 --> 01:01:33,206
-Dave's van's
parked right in back.

1528
01:01:33,241 --> 01:01:36,485
Can't miss it.
-I will be there.

1529
01:01:36,520 --> 01:01:38,177
-You're not going.
-I said get out of my way!

1530
01:01:38,211 --> 01:01:40,386
-And I said you're not going!

1531
01:01:40,420 --> 01:01:43,147
-Oh. It's discipline time.

1532
01:01:43,182 --> 01:01:45,046
Johnny, go to your room.

1533
01:01:45,080 --> 01:01:48,705
♪♪

1534
01:01:48,739 --> 01:01:52,847
♪ Peeking through the knothole
in grandma's wooden leg ♪

1535
01:01:52,881 --> 01:01:56,747
♪ Where do the build the shore
so near the ocean? ♪

1536
01:01:56,782 --> 01:02:01,027
[Humming]

1537
01:02:01,062 --> 01:02:02,822
Oh, excuse me.

1538
01:02:02,857 --> 01:02:04,513
Did it again. Pulled my finger.

1539
01:02:04,548 --> 01:02:06,343
Pulled my own finger. [Chuckles]

1540
01:02:06,377 --> 01:02:12,176
♪♪

1541
01:02:12,211 --> 01:02:14,144
-Hey, it's an old film
of Bigfoot.

1542
01:02:14,178 --> 01:02:16,905
-Oh, yeah, we shall add me one
of those all-terrain vehicles.

1543
01:02:16,940 --> 01:02:19,839
I'm getting a little too big
to climb these planets.

1544
01:02:19,874 --> 01:02:22,186
♪♪

1545
01:02:22,221 --> 01:02:24,154
-Johnny!

1546
01:02:24,188 --> 01:02:26,397
Johnny!

1547
01:02:26,432 --> 01:02:28,745
Johnny's gone!

1548
01:02:28,779 --> 01:02:30,712
-You don't think
he'd be outside the back?

1549
01:02:30,747 --> 01:02:32,818
-No.
That kid would try anything!

1550
01:02:32,852 --> 01:02:34,371
What a family I have!

1551
01:02:34,405 --> 01:02:36,028
-I didn't do anything.

1552
01:02:36,062 --> 01:02:38,168
-Johnny has left the barricade.

1553
01:02:38,202 --> 01:02:40,549
He might have it in his head
to find Ro-Man.

1554
01:02:40,584 --> 01:02:42,862
We have to stop him.
-Don't worry, professor.

1555
01:02:42,897 --> 01:02:45,175
Alice and I can find him.
-I'll go, of course.

1556
01:02:45,209 --> 01:02:47,004
But don't either of you
speak to me.

1557
01:02:47,039 --> 01:02:49,041
-Little boy who crumbled
the Ro-Man empire.

1558
01:02:49,075 --> 01:02:51,043
-If Johnny comes back,
I will set off a flare.

1559
01:02:51,077 --> 01:02:54,218
-And kill the fatted calf.

1560
01:02:54,253 --> 01:02:57,670
♪♪

1561
01:02:57,704 --> 01:03:00,880
-♪ Oh, three Irishmen,
three Irishmen ♪

1562
01:03:00,915 --> 01:03:03,987
[Humming]

1563
01:03:04,021 --> 01:03:06,713
♪ What's so fun,
the planet Earth ♪

1564
01:03:06,748 --> 01:03:08,681
Excuse me. [Chuckles]

1565
01:03:08,715 --> 01:03:10,096
[Humming]

1566
01:03:10,131 --> 01:03:13,341
♪♪

1567
01:03:13,375 --> 01:03:15,515
-Ben!

1568
01:03:15,550 --> 01:03:17,448
Ben!

1569
01:03:17,483 --> 01:03:19,519
-It's a good Clint Howard
impression.

1570
01:03:19,554 --> 01:03:22,005
I like that.
-Huh?

1571
01:03:22,039 --> 01:03:24,007
-I got the eyebrows for it.

1572
01:03:24,041 --> 01:03:34,017
♪♪

1573
01:03:34,051 --> 01:03:37,675
♪♪

1574
01:03:37,710 --> 01:03:40,057
-What, is Ro-Man on the parade
of homes?

1575
01:03:40,092 --> 01:03:42,542
♪♪

1576
01:03:42,577 --> 01:03:43,716
-He's just roamin' around.

1577
01:03:43,750 --> 01:03:45,856
-What are you doing here, boy?

1578
01:03:45,891 --> 01:03:48,203
-My sister isn't coming.

1579
01:03:48,238 --> 01:03:50,136
-So they sent you?

1580
01:03:50,171 --> 01:03:51,655
-I came by myself.

1581
01:03:51,689 --> 01:03:54,037
I wanted to find out
what you had against me.

1582
01:03:54,071 --> 01:03:55,901
-Your voice, for starters.
-You are human.

1583
01:03:55,935 --> 01:03:58,041
Your people were getting
too intelligent.

1584
01:03:58,075 --> 01:04:00,940
We could not wait until you werestrong enough to attack us.

1585
01:04:00,975 --> 01:04:02,908
We had to attack you first.

1586
01:04:02,942 --> 01:04:04,668
-I think you're just
a big bully,

1587
01:04:04,702 --> 01:04:07,291
picking on people
smaller than you are.

1588
01:04:07,326 --> 01:04:09,155
-Now I will kill you.

1589
01:04:09,190 --> 01:04:10,881
-That did it.

1590
01:04:10,916 --> 01:04:12,676
She is a big bully.

1591
01:04:12,710 --> 01:04:14,643
[Electricity crackling]

1592
01:04:14,678 --> 01:04:16,576
-Kill first,
ask questions later.

1593
01:04:16,611 --> 01:04:19,131
-You look like
a pooped-out pinwheel!

1594
01:04:19,165 --> 01:04:22,168
-Oh, come here
and say that, you kid!

1595
01:04:22,203 --> 01:04:24,895
-...really cannot harm you.

1596
01:04:24,930 --> 01:04:27,518
Your father must be
a brilliant scientist.

1597
01:04:27,553 --> 01:04:28,726
-He's got a super serum

1598
01:04:28,761 --> 01:04:30,867
that keeps people
from ever getting sick.

1599
01:04:30,901 --> 01:04:33,041
-Maple serum?
-How do you know it works?

1600
01:04:33,076 --> 01:04:35,664
-Because he tried it on me
and Carla and Allison,

1601
01:04:35,699 --> 01:04:37,528
Roy, and everybody.
-Shh.

1602
01:04:37,563 --> 01:04:39,737
-And we don't get sick,
even when we swallow capsules

1603
01:04:39,772 --> 01:04:41,222
with real bad bugs in them.

1604
01:04:41,256 --> 01:04:42,568
-Maybe you should stop
eating bugs anyway.

1605
01:04:42,602 --> 01:04:44,018
-And the two men who took off
on the rocket ship,

1606
01:04:44,052 --> 01:04:46,434
they also had this injection?
-Sure.

1607
01:04:46,468 --> 01:04:47,538
They -- [Gasps]

1608
01:04:47,573 --> 01:04:50,162
-Oh, he's singing like a canary.

1609
01:04:50,196 --> 01:04:52,958
-I will calculate the spectrum
dust and account a death ray

1610
01:04:52,992 --> 01:04:55,167
to counteract this antibiotic.

1611
01:04:55,201 --> 01:04:56,893
-Hey, how did you hear
about my Auntie Biotic?

1612
01:04:56,927 --> 01:04:59,240
-It was a Uncle Biotic.

1613
01:04:59,274 --> 01:05:01,138
-And all the little biotics.

1614
01:05:01,173 --> 01:05:03,140
-[Laughs] The biotic man.

1615
01:05:03,175 --> 01:05:05,142
-Come back here, you rotten kid.

1616
01:05:05,177 --> 01:05:08,628
I'm going to shake my fist
at you, old boy!

1617
01:05:08,663 --> 01:05:10,147
-What's so scary about an alien

1618
01:05:10,182 --> 01:05:12,632
that looks like the mascot
of a college football team?

1619
01:05:12,667 --> 01:05:14,220
-He must be from Texas A&M.

1620
01:05:14,255 --> 01:05:17,154
You know, ape and monster.

1621
01:05:17,189 --> 01:05:18,707
[Laughter]

1622
01:05:18,742 --> 01:05:21,055
-Hit him!
-Oh!

1623
01:05:21,089 --> 01:05:23,989
That didn't hurt.

1624
01:05:24,023 --> 01:05:25,507
-Hmm.

1625
01:05:25,542 --> 01:05:28,338
You know, it's really quite nicewhen you get used to it.

1626
01:05:28,372 --> 01:05:30,478
♪♪

1627
01:05:30,512 --> 01:05:35,172
-The hills are alive with
the sound of weird music.

1628
01:05:35,207 --> 01:05:38,865
-Ah, this is what
we've been waiting for.

1629
01:05:38,900 --> 01:05:42,179
-Try to stay on camera,
everybody.

1630
01:05:42,214 --> 01:05:45,217
-[Humming]

1631
01:05:45,251 --> 01:05:46,873
♪♪

1632
01:05:46,908 --> 01:05:49,186
-Oh, right, she can walk,
but she can't run.

1633
01:05:49,221 --> 01:05:51,016
-It's just that
her knees give out

1634
01:05:51,050 --> 01:05:53,742
when she sees a robot monster.

1635
01:05:53,777 --> 01:05:56,021
-She can't eat. She can't sleep.

1636
01:05:56,055 --> 01:05:57,884
All she wants to do
is think about him,

1637
01:05:57,919 --> 01:06:00,887
be with him, groom him.

1638
01:06:00,922 --> 01:06:08,274
♪♪

1639
01:06:08,309 --> 01:06:09,827
[Electricity crackling]

1640
01:06:09,862 --> 01:06:12,313
-No more static out of you,
buddy!

1641
01:06:12,347 --> 01:06:17,007
♪♪

1642
01:06:17,042 --> 01:06:19,182
-Just duck down here
in the bunker.

1643
01:06:19,216 --> 01:06:22,012
He looks like
a walking paintbrush.

1644
01:06:22,047 --> 01:06:24,497
-Well, maybe he's from
that Sherwin-Williams planet.

1645
01:06:24,532 --> 01:06:26,844
You know, the one
that's covered with paint.

1646
01:06:26,879 --> 01:06:36,164
♪♪

1647
01:06:36,199 --> 01:06:39,892
[Electricity crackling]

1648
01:06:39,926 --> 01:06:42,032
-Stop beating around the bush.

1649
01:06:42,067 --> 01:06:43,482
-You know, he kind of looks like

1650
01:06:43,516 --> 01:06:47,348
Baloo the Bear from
the "Jungle Book."

1651
01:06:47,382 --> 01:06:49,350
Those -- Those ape necessities.

1652
01:06:49,384 --> 01:06:51,697
-Robot monster necessities?

1653
01:06:51,731 --> 01:06:53,526
♪♪

1654
01:06:53,561 --> 01:06:56,667
[Electricity crackling]

1655
01:07:00,706 --> 01:07:01,983
-Ann?

1656
01:07:02,018 --> 01:07:03,467
-Judge! Judge!

1657
01:07:03,502 --> 01:07:06,125
There he is! He looks all right!

1658
01:07:06,160 --> 01:07:08,817
-Run! -Run, Van Ryan!

1659
01:07:08,852 --> 01:07:12,994
- Run, Van Ryan!
-[Speaks German]

1660
01:07:13,029 --> 01:07:14,616
Come into the bunker!

1661
01:07:21,554 --> 01:07:23,625
-You became one of them.

1662
01:07:23,660 --> 01:07:25,282
-I was just
standing next to them.

1663
01:07:25,317 --> 01:07:27,319
-Hey, did you bring the chips?

1664
01:07:27,353 --> 01:07:29,252
Where's the salsa?

1665
01:07:29,286 --> 01:07:30,805
Looks like he spilled
the sour cream.

1666
01:07:30,839 --> 01:07:32,324
-Empty-handed again.

1667
01:07:32,358 --> 01:07:34,878
-Hey, always wipe your feet
before entering a bunker.

1668
01:07:34,912 --> 01:07:36,362
-It's all right.

1669
01:07:36,397 --> 01:07:38,192
Now, tell us all about it.

1670
01:07:38,226 --> 01:07:41,195
-No it isn't, Mom.
I gave it all away.

1671
01:07:41,229 --> 01:07:42,955
I didn't mean to, but I did.

1672
01:07:42,989 --> 01:07:44,198
-You did what?

1673
01:07:44,232 --> 01:07:46,959
-I wanted to talk to Ro-Man,
but he got out of me

1674
01:07:46,993 --> 01:07:49,168
how we were protected
from the death ray.

1675
01:07:49,203 --> 01:07:51,481
And now he's going to
do something about it.

1676
01:07:51,515 --> 01:07:53,138
-Now he's going to sue us.
-It's all right, boy.

1677
01:07:53,172 --> 01:07:54,725
You did right.

1678
01:07:54,760 --> 01:07:58,695
And Ro-Man won't find it easy
to counteract the serum,

1679
01:07:58,729 --> 01:08:01,456
so we have still
a little time left.

1680
01:08:01,491 --> 01:08:03,596
-Butterscotch serum?
-I only wish it were over now.

1681
01:08:03,631 --> 01:08:04,977
-This is getting a little old,
isn't it?

1682
01:08:05,011 --> 01:08:06,979
-Well, when it is, can I go overto Janie's house

1683
01:08:07,013 --> 01:08:09,464
and borrow her dolls?
-Yeah, sure.

1684
01:08:09,499 --> 01:08:12,260
Of course!
-You're one sick puppy, kid.

1685
01:08:18,335 --> 01:08:20,475
-Solar flares
at the end of the earth.

1686
01:08:20,510 --> 01:08:23,478
-Shh, Ro-Man might hear us!

1687
01:08:23,513 --> 01:08:27,931
-Even at the end of the world,
love springs eternal.

1688
01:08:27,965 --> 01:08:31,072
Man needs woman to be his steed.

1689
01:08:31,107 --> 01:08:32,349
Woman needs man.

1690
01:08:32,384 --> 01:08:34,662
Yeah. Now she got the need.

1691
01:08:34,696 --> 01:08:36,974
-Is that right, Joel?

1692
01:08:37,009 --> 01:08:38,148
-I think
it's something like that.

1693
01:08:38,183 --> 01:08:39,632
It's an old Alice Cooper song.

1694
01:08:39,667 --> 01:08:42,014
-Hey!

1695
01:08:42,048 --> 01:08:46,156
-[Humming]

1696
01:08:46,191 --> 01:08:48,158
♪♪

1697
01:08:48,193 --> 01:08:50,471
-He's bleeding from the ear.

1698
01:08:50,505 --> 01:08:53,336
-Must be good.
-It's that little kids voice.

1699
01:08:53,370 --> 01:09:00,481
♪♪

1700
01:09:00,515 --> 01:09:02,483
-Maybe it's an earring.

1701
01:09:02,517 --> 01:09:04,588
-[Sighs]

1702
01:09:04,623 --> 01:09:07,004
-[Humming]

1703
01:09:07,039 --> 01:09:09,283
-Oh, he deflowered her!
-That's nothing.

1704
01:09:09,317 --> 01:09:11,147
See the sun, honey? Up there?

1705
01:09:11,181 --> 01:09:12,838
Way back.
That sun means nothing.

1706
01:09:12,872 --> 01:09:15,012
But you -- you are something.

1707
01:09:15,047 --> 01:09:16,980
Yeah. You are something, girl.
Yep!

1708
01:09:17,014 --> 01:09:18,395
Well, I feel the same way
about you,

1709
01:09:18,430 --> 01:09:19,810
your forehead and everything,

1710
01:09:19,845 --> 01:09:24,988
but it's gloomy, and, well,
wait a minute, you are big.

1711
01:09:25,022 --> 01:09:28,440
Whereas, me, well, uh,
I'm small. Yeah.

1712
01:09:28,474 --> 01:09:31,684
Oh, honey,
you're my kind of gal.

1713
01:09:31,719 --> 01:09:32,892
Oh!

1714
01:09:32,927 --> 01:09:34,825
-[Sighs]

1715
01:09:34,860 --> 01:09:37,000
-I'm misty now, Joel.
That was beautiful.

1716
01:09:37,034 --> 01:09:39,175
-I feel so real.

1717
01:09:39,209 --> 01:09:41,004
-I feel used.

1718
01:09:41,038 --> 01:09:43,317
-I'm defenseless. Yes.

1719
01:09:43,351 --> 01:09:45,319
Let's go to a commercial.

1720
01:09:45,353 --> 01:09:54,362
♪♪

1721
01:09:54,397 --> 01:09:57,848
-Here comes
Romping Rowdy Ro-Man!

1722
01:09:57,883 --> 01:10:02,336
♪♪

1723
01:10:02,370 --> 01:10:04,855
[Electricity crackling]

1724
01:10:04,890 --> 01:10:06,650
-While Mommy
braided Cindy's hair,

1725
01:10:06,685 --> 01:10:10,344
Daddy read from the home repair
and improvement bunker guide.

1726
01:10:10,378 --> 01:10:14,244
-You know, we could put
a ceiling on this place.

1727
01:10:14,279 --> 01:10:17,178
-Who's got the time?
It's the end of the earth.

1728
01:10:18,524 --> 01:10:21,320
-There's always time
for a good roof.

1729
01:10:21,355 --> 01:10:23,080
-Catch!

1730
01:10:23,115 --> 01:10:25,013
-Oh!

1731
01:10:28,189 --> 01:10:30,122
What has kept you two?

1732
01:10:30,156 --> 01:10:31,330
-Well, you know.

1733
01:10:31,365 --> 01:10:33,505
-Not really, father.
Isn't it obvious?

1734
01:10:33,539 --> 01:10:35,369
-Have you been playing house?

1735
01:10:35,403 --> 01:10:36,887
-In a way. In a way.

1736
01:10:36,922 --> 01:10:39,373
-Professor, uh,
it may sound silly to you,

1737
01:10:39,407 --> 01:10:41,202
but Alice and I
want to get married.

1738
01:10:41,237 --> 01:10:42,859
And we were wondering
how you'd feel

1739
01:10:42,893 --> 01:10:44,757
about performing the ceremony?

1740
01:10:44,792 --> 01:10:46,966
-You want me to?
-Oh, yes!

1741
01:10:47,001 --> 01:10:49,624
-In that case, let's do it!

1742
01:10:49,659 --> 01:10:50,970
And I want you to know,

1743
01:10:51,005 --> 01:10:53,525
this is the biggest
social event of the year!

1744
01:10:53,559 --> 01:10:55,216
-It's the only social event
of the year.

1745
01:10:55,251 --> 01:10:57,425
It's the last social event
of the year.

1746
01:10:57,460 --> 01:10:58,737
We know.

1747
01:10:58,771 --> 01:11:00,117
-Meanwhile, at the Mundy house,

1748
01:11:00,152 --> 01:11:04,018
Baloo had just awaken
from a long winter's nap.

1749
01:11:04,052 --> 01:11:08,367
-I just took a tick bath, and Ican't do a thing with this pelt.

1750
01:11:08,402 --> 01:11:09,920
-Think he's going to get jealous

1751
01:11:09,955 --> 01:11:13,648
that Alice is going to
get married to another guy?

1752
01:11:13,683 --> 01:11:16,686
-Only time will tell.

1753
01:11:16,720 --> 01:11:20,206
-It's going to be like thecurly knife scene in "Oklahoma."

1754
01:11:20,241 --> 01:11:22,485
-Come in, same guy.

1755
01:11:22,519 --> 01:11:24,832
♪♪

1756
01:11:24,866 --> 01:11:27,697
-Great Guidance,
I have discovered the secret

1757
01:11:27,731 --> 01:11:30,216
of our failureto destroy the remaining humans.

1758
01:11:30,251 --> 01:11:32,736
-It's these gorilla suits.
They really slow me down!

1759
01:11:32,771 --> 01:11:35,360
-Our C ray,
the Calcinator Death Ray,

1760
01:11:35,394 --> 01:11:36,947
cannot penetrate them.

1761
01:11:36,982 --> 01:11:39,847
They have been made immune
to the antibiotic serum,

1762
01:11:39,881 --> 01:11:44,092
which I believe is the same
as our formula, XZA.

1763
01:11:44,127 --> 01:11:45,646
-Or janitor in a drum.

1764
01:11:45,680 --> 01:11:47,199
-Eliminate the error!

1765
01:11:47,233 --> 01:11:50,098
Death to humans
can come by force.

1766
01:11:50,133 --> 01:11:51,514
-Remember your S training.

1767
01:11:51,548 --> 01:11:53,550
-...physical means, Great One.

1768
01:11:53,585 --> 01:11:56,484
The plan shall be fulfilled.

1769
01:11:56,519 --> 01:11:58,762
The planet earth
has half revolved.

1770
01:11:58,797 --> 01:12:02,490
You have but a short time
to achieve our goal.

1771
01:12:02,525 --> 01:12:05,942
♪♪

1772
01:12:05,976 --> 01:12:08,496
