Mine is in the cave.

2026
01:23:17,199 --> 01:23:19,201
-The cave? Hmm?

2027
01:23:19,235 --> 01:23:20,685
♪♪

2028
01:23:20,719 --> 01:23:22,721
-I wish now I played house
with her more often

2029
01:23:22,756 --> 01:23:24,033
when she wanted to.

2030
01:23:24,068 --> 01:23:25,517
-Shut up,
you little insensitive dolt!

2031
01:23:25,552 --> 01:23:26,691
-Don't be sad, Johnny.

2032
01:23:26,725 --> 01:23:28,520
We enjoyed her
as long as she was with us,

2033
01:23:28,555 --> 01:23:32,179
and now, somehow, we have to
find a way to live without her.

2034
01:23:32,214 --> 01:23:34,354
-Is this the Donner party story?

2035
01:23:34,388 --> 01:23:35,872
-Yeah, Donner Reed.

2036
01:23:35,907 --> 01:23:37,012
-Oh!
-Oh!

2037
01:23:37,046 --> 01:23:38,358
-I did it again.

2038
01:23:38,392 --> 01:23:40,877
Sorry.

2039
01:23:40,912 --> 01:23:42,948
-Mash me up
and call me a potato.

2040
01:23:42,983 --> 01:23:45,917
-There's a robot monster robot,
big robot helmet!

2041
01:23:45,951 --> 01:23:48,023
Robot!
-Ro-Man's -- Ro-Man's --

2042
01:23:48,057 --> 01:23:49,679
-Robot monster.

2043
01:23:49,714 --> 01:23:53,338
-Start another grave, dear.
-[Screaming]

2044
01:23:53,373 --> 01:23:54,891
-Am I your first Ro-Man?

2045
01:23:54,926 --> 01:23:56,341
Let me show you
what I've got down --

2046
01:23:56,376 --> 01:23:57,584
uh,
what I've done with the cave.

2047
01:23:57,618 --> 01:23:59,206
It's very romantic.
You're going to love it.

2048
01:23:59,241 --> 01:24:01,070
You know, I've got mirrors
on the stalactites,

2049
01:24:01,105 --> 01:24:03,383
and I got a new CD player.

2050
01:24:03,417 --> 01:24:06,041
-Roy is dead!

2051
01:24:06,075 --> 01:24:09,044
And nothing can be done.

2052
01:24:09,078 --> 01:24:10,493
-Roy's dead.
The little girl is dead.

2053
01:24:10,528 --> 01:24:12,530
-Maybe one of us could
lure him out for a moment

2054
01:24:12,564 --> 01:24:14,980
and the others
could run in and grab Alice.

2055
01:24:15,015 --> 01:24:16,844
-Hey!
-That's easier said than done.

2056
01:24:16,879 --> 01:24:19,675
-He'd come if he could be sure
of killing us.

2057
01:24:19,709 --> 01:24:20,814
-Go on! Go on!

2058
01:24:20,848 --> 01:24:22,643
-Tell me more.
-I like it!

2059
01:24:22,678 --> 01:24:24,162
-Call him on the viewer screen.

2060
01:24:24,197 --> 01:24:26,130
Tell him we don't want
to fight anymore.

2061
01:24:26,164 --> 01:24:27,648
-Uh-huh.
-He can get us in the ravine

2062
01:24:27,683 --> 01:24:29,581
if he promises easy death.
-Uh-huh.

2063
01:24:29,616 --> 01:24:30,996
And then he kills us, right?

2064
01:24:31,031 --> 01:24:33,516
-You slip in and grab Alice
when he comes out after me.

2065
01:24:33,551 --> 01:24:35,863
-It might work!
He has no time to lose.

2066
01:24:35,898 --> 01:24:38,694
-I like it!

2067
01:24:38,728 --> 01:24:41,662
Mother, keep digging graves.
Better do two.

2068
01:24:41,697 --> 01:24:44,044
This isn't going too well.

2069
01:24:44,079 --> 01:24:46,046
-Little one, big one.

2070
01:24:46,081 --> 01:24:49,153
-You know, and I got the whole
Cowsils collection on -- on CD.

2071
01:24:49,187 --> 01:24:51,396
It's going to be great.
You're going to love it.

2072
01:24:51,431 --> 01:24:53,088
-Hands off the merchandise, pal!

2073
01:24:53,122 --> 01:24:55,055
You overgrown dust bunny.

2074
01:24:55,090 --> 01:25:00,095
♪♪

2075
01:25:00,129 --> 01:25:06,135
-Suppose I were human,
would you treat me like a man?

2076
01:25:06,170 --> 01:25:08,482
-He's been using
the view screen.

2077
01:25:08,517 --> 01:25:10,864
-Hey!
-Now cut that out!

2078
01:25:10,898 --> 01:25:14,178
I don't like you alien types
touching our women folk.

2079
01:25:14,212 --> 01:25:16,835
-Silence, girl!

2080
01:25:16,870 --> 01:25:18,768
-That's it! That's it!

2081
01:25:18,803 --> 01:25:20,322
You come --

2082
01:25:20,356 --> 01:25:22,013
[High-pitched whining]

2083
01:25:22,047 --> 01:25:24,671
Oh. You. Talkin' to you.

2084
01:25:24,705 --> 01:25:28,157
That's better.

2085
01:25:28,192 --> 01:25:30,332
-Oh, no!

2086
01:25:30,366 --> 01:25:34,232
He's fitting her
for a gorilla suit.

2087
01:25:34,267 --> 01:25:36,855
Girl-illa.

2088
01:25:36,890 --> 01:25:38,478
-Stop it.

2089
01:25:38,512 --> 01:25:40,583
Oh, nice tag!

2090
01:25:40,618 --> 01:25:42,137
Nice swoon.

2091
01:25:42,171 --> 01:25:43,690
-Nice fall.

2092
01:25:43,724 --> 01:25:46,382
♪♪

2093
01:25:46,417 --> 01:25:48,177
-Look, I'm really busy
right now.

2094
01:25:48,212 --> 01:25:50,869
If you can call back,
I'd really appreciate it.

2095
01:25:50,904 --> 01:25:53,148
♪♪

2096
01:25:53,182 --> 01:25:55,495
-Why do you call me
at this time?

2097
01:25:55,529 --> 01:25:56,496
-Ro-Man?

2098
01:25:56,530 --> 01:25:59,568
We can't stand it any longer.

2099
01:25:59,602 --> 01:26:01,984
-I have made my last offer.

2100
01:26:02,018 --> 01:26:07,127
-You promised us a painless
death if we give ourselves up.

2101
01:26:07,162 --> 01:26:08,646
Come and get us!

2102
01:26:08,680 --> 01:26:11,925
-You can wait.
Call me again at another time.

2103
01:26:11,959 --> 01:26:13,306
-No!
-I'm kind of busy right now.

2104
01:26:13,340 --> 01:26:16,619
-We'll meet you halfway,
in the ravine.

2105
01:26:16,654 --> 01:26:17,827
-All right.

2106
01:26:17,862 --> 01:26:19,139
I will meet you in the ravine

2107
01:26:19,174 --> 01:26:22,694
when the sun passes
over the mountains.

2108
01:26:22,729 --> 01:26:24,662
-Oh, so night?

2109
01:26:24,696 --> 01:26:34,672
♪♪

2110
01:26:34,706 --> 01:26:37,847
♪♪

2111
01:26:37,882 --> 01:26:39,332
-Did she tie herself up?

2112
01:26:39,366 --> 01:26:42,680
♪♪

2113
01:26:42,714 --> 01:26:44,199
[High-pitched whining]

2114
01:26:44,233 --> 01:26:45,579
-Oh, what is it now?

2115
01:26:45,614 --> 01:26:47,857
Every time I find
an Earth girl I like,

2116
01:26:47,892 --> 01:26:51,654
I get a phone call,
Ro-Man this, Ro-Man that.

2117
01:26:51,689 --> 01:26:52,966
-Kill the human!

2118
01:26:53,000 --> 01:26:59,662
♪♪

2119
01:26:59,697 --> 01:27:01,768
-Attention!

2120
01:27:01,802 --> 01:27:05,806
Attention! Extension XJ2!

2121
01:27:05,841 --> 01:27:07,774
-Attention extension.
-Attention!

2122
01:27:07,808 --> 01:27:10,639
Attention! Extension XJ2!

2123
01:27:10,673 --> 01:27:12,813
-Hey, I'm up to my armpits
in humans down here.

2124
01:27:12,848 --> 01:27:14,988
The painters are in.
I can't fill half these orders.

2125
01:27:15,022 --> 01:27:16,092
Look at me!

2126
01:27:16,127 --> 01:27:17,922
I'm a wreck!
-Violate the law of plan.

2127
01:27:17,956 --> 01:27:19,199
Fact.

2128
01:27:19,234 --> 01:27:22,167
You have captured the girl
and not destroyed her.

2129
01:27:22,202 --> 01:27:23,652
Fact!
-Fact!

2130
01:27:23,686 --> 01:27:25,861
-You have delayed accepting
the surround of the others.

2131
01:27:25,895 --> 01:27:28,208
This verges on failure.

2132
01:27:28,243 --> 01:27:32,108
-There is one thing you do
not understand, Great Guidance.

2133
01:27:32,143 --> 01:27:35,077
-You reject the plan?

2134
01:27:35,111 --> 01:27:38,805
-I wish to make an estimate
of my own.

2135
01:27:38,839 --> 01:27:42,291
-To think for yourself
is to be like the human!

2136
01:27:42,326 --> 01:27:44,328
-Me-man?
-Yes.

2137
01:27:44,362 --> 01:27:46,191
To be like the human.

2138
01:27:46,226 --> 01:27:48,677
To laugh, feel, want.

2139
01:27:48,711 --> 01:27:51,335
Why are these things
not in the plan?

2140
01:27:51,369 --> 01:27:53,751
-You are an extension
of the Ro-Man.

2141
01:27:53,785 --> 01:27:56,201
And the Ro-Man you will remain.

2142
01:27:56,236 --> 01:27:58,203
Now I set you into motion.

2143
01:27:58,238 --> 01:28:00,309
One, destroy the girl.

2144
01:28:00,344 --> 01:28:02,898
Two, destroy the family!

2145
01:28:02,932 --> 01:28:05,590
Fail, and I will destroy you!

2146
01:28:05,625 --> 01:28:07,799
-Uh, what's number three?

2147
01:28:07,834 --> 01:28:09,836
Do I get a choice?

2148
01:28:09,870 --> 01:28:12,528
-Do not violate ape law!

2149
01:28:12,563 --> 01:28:14,634
-What a touching little scene.

2150
01:28:14,668 --> 01:28:17,326
-I cannot, yet I must.

2151
01:28:17,361 --> 01:28:19,466
How do you calculate that?

2152
01:28:19,501 --> 01:28:23,367
At what point on the graph
do "must" and "cannot" meet?

2153
01:28:23,401 --> 01:28:24,885
Yet I must.

2154
01:28:24,920 --> 01:28:25,955
But I cannot.

2155
01:28:25,990 --> 01:28:28,993
-But you cannot.
-This guy is deep.

2156
01:28:29,027 --> 01:28:31,616
-That's a touching soliloquy.
-He's deep.

2157
01:28:31,651 --> 01:28:33,411
And thick!

2158
01:28:33,446 --> 01:28:35,724
-He's furry.

2159
01:28:35,758 --> 01:28:40,245
♪♪

2160
01:28:40,280 --> 01:28:43,179
-Now, son,
this is the first thing --

2161
01:28:43,214 --> 01:28:44,871
time you've been away from home

2162
01:28:44,905 --> 01:28:46,666
luring the destroyer
of the world

2163
01:28:46,700 --> 01:28:49,634
out of his lair
to save what's left of mankind,

2164
01:28:49,669 --> 01:28:52,499
so I want you to keep
a cheerful disposition

2165
01:28:52,534 --> 01:28:53,983
and remember to wash up.

2166
01:28:54,018 --> 01:28:57,332
And I want you to take this hairdryer with you for safekeeping.

2167
01:28:57,366 --> 01:29:00,093
Now, your mother and I will get
safely away from the blast zone

2168
01:29:00,127 --> 01:29:01,819
and really have
a wonderful time.

2169
01:29:01,853 --> 01:29:03,786
-Write if you get work! [Laughs]

2170
01:29:03,821 --> 01:29:06,064
-Oh, what's that kid going to dowith a hot glue gun,

2171
01:29:06,099 --> 01:29:09,136
stick the ape's pelt
to the cave wall?

2172
01:29:09,171 --> 01:29:18,318
♪♪

2173
01:29:18,353 --> 01:29:19,457
-Attention.

2174
01:29:19,492 --> 01:29:22,978
Attention, Extension XJ2.

2175
01:29:23,012 --> 01:29:25,394
-Attention. Extension.

2176
01:29:25,429 --> 01:29:27,465
-Put him on hold.

2177
01:29:27,500 --> 01:29:31,331
Ben! Ben! Ben!

2178
01:29:31,366 --> 01:29:34,092
♪♪

2179
01:29:34,127 --> 01:29:36,198
-Speak, Great Guidance.

2180
01:29:36,232 --> 01:29:38,407
-Why have you not
killed the girl?

2181
01:29:38,442 --> 01:29:40,961
-I must, but I cannot.

2182
01:29:40,996 --> 01:29:43,032
-I couldn't kill her.

2183
01:29:43,067 --> 01:29:44,827
They cut away to the scene
with the humans,

2184
01:29:44,862 --> 01:29:46,484
and I can only
kill her on camera.

2185
01:29:46,519 --> 01:29:48,244
-Here I am, Ro-Man!

2186
01:29:48,279 --> 01:29:50,661
-This monkey is in love.

2187
01:29:50,695 --> 01:29:53,249
-Girl first, then the boy now!
-Great Guidance...

2188
01:29:53,284 --> 01:29:55,493
-What? The girl is tied up.
She's not going anywhere.

2189
01:29:55,528 --> 01:29:57,599
-...kill the girl,
but I will kill the boy.

2190
01:29:57,633 --> 01:29:59,670
-Here I am!

2191
01:29:59,704 --> 01:30:01,016
♪♪

2192
01:30:01,050 --> 01:30:03,984
-Alice, do not hate me.

2193
01:30:04,019 --> 01:30:06,021
I must.

2194
01:30:06,055 --> 01:30:09,265
-[Humming]

2195
01:30:09,300 --> 01:30:17,481
♪♪

2196
01:30:17,515 --> 01:30:19,966
-Bet it really smells
in that cave.

2197
01:30:20,000 --> 01:30:22,520
[Electricity crackling]

2198
01:30:22,555 --> 01:30:25,937
-♪ Peeking through the knothole
In Grandma's wooden leg, oh ♪

2199
01:30:25,972 --> 01:30:27,456
-I've hired an idiot.

2200
01:30:27,491 --> 01:30:31,978
♪♪

2201
01:30:32,012 --> 01:30:35,947
-Lovely, lovely.

2202
01:30:35,982 --> 01:30:38,536
-You wish to be a human. Good.

2203
01:30:38,571 --> 01:30:40,262
You can die a human.

2204
01:30:40,296 --> 01:30:42,057
-Whoa! Whoa!

2205
01:30:42,091 --> 01:30:45,232
[Electricity crackles]

2206
01:30:45,267 --> 01:30:47,200
-Well, uh, save the suit,
at least.

2207
01:30:47,234 --> 01:30:48,581
It's rented.

2208
01:30:48,615 --> 01:30:50,410
Yeah.

2209
01:30:50,445 --> 01:30:57,486
♪♪

2210
01:30:57,521 --> 01:30:59,764
-Human elements
still roam planet Earth.

2211
01:30:59,799 --> 01:31:01,870
I, the ruler of all Ro-Mans...
-A different voice.

2212
01:31:01,904 --> 01:31:05,045
-...shall complete your task,
Earth Ro-Man.

2213
01:31:05,080 --> 01:31:07,496
I shall release
our cosmic Q-rays.

2214
01:31:07,531 --> 01:31:08,980
[Electricity crackles]

2215
01:31:09,015 --> 01:31:10,361
Which will bring...

2216
01:31:10,395 --> 01:31:13,191
-Uh, cue the deus ex machina.

2217
01:31:13,226 --> 01:31:15,608
-...to devour
whatever remains of life.

2218
01:31:15,642 --> 01:31:18,127
-"Deus ex machine-a," isn't it?

2219
01:31:18,162 --> 01:31:21,545
-You say, "Machine-a,"
I say, "Mack-ina."

2220
01:31:21,579 --> 01:31:24,686
-Let's call the whole line off.

2221
01:31:24,720 --> 01:31:25,721
-Kitty!

2222
01:31:25,756 --> 01:31:28,931
-It's a Play-Doh fun set
come to life,

2223
01:31:28,966 --> 01:31:30,899
the magic of claymation.

2224
01:31:30,933 --> 01:31:32,417
-Triceratops.

2225
01:31:32,452 --> 01:31:34,523
-Okay, but I usually
don't like ceratops.

2226
01:31:34,558 --> 01:31:37,526
-Cyclotronic vibrations
will smash the planet Earth

2227
01:31:37,561 --> 01:31:40,391
out of the universe!
-Oh, come on.

2228
01:31:40,425 --> 01:31:42,393
We've seen this.

2229
01:31:42,427 --> 01:31:45,534
-Oh. Ew!

2230
01:31:45,569 --> 01:31:48,399
- It's Gecko-Ro-Man wrestling.
-Ugh.

2231
01:31:48,433 --> 01:31:50,090
Alligator turnover.

2232
01:31:50,125 --> 01:31:52,714
Most taste like chicken
to each other.

2233
01:31:52,748 --> 01:31:54,647
[Electricity crackles]

2234
01:31:54,681 --> 01:31:57,442
♪♪

2235
01:31:57,477 --> 01:31:59,583
-Well, that looks real.

2236
01:31:59,617 --> 01:32:01,343
That doesn't.

2237
01:32:01,377 --> 01:32:03,345
♪♪

2238
01:32:03,379 --> 01:32:05,450
Must be pretty good
lizard glue they used

2239
01:32:05,485 --> 01:32:07,314
to put that fin on that gator.

2240
01:32:07,349 --> 01:32:16,392
♪♪

2241
01:32:16,427 --> 01:32:19,499
-Aren't they supposed to
fight the humans?

2242
01:32:19,534 --> 01:32:20,604
-There are no humans.

2243
01:32:20,638 --> 01:32:23,020
This is from
an entirely different film.

2244
01:32:23,054 --> 01:32:24,849
-Yeah.

2245
01:32:24,884 --> 01:32:29,060
[Electricity crackles]

2246
01:32:29,095 --> 01:32:32,374
-There goes the, uh,
Tyco railroad scenery.

2247
01:32:32,408 --> 01:32:34,410
-Sort of a shame to see it breaklike that.

2248
01:32:34,445 --> 01:32:36,343
-Take it easy, son.
You're all right.

2249
01:32:36,378 --> 01:32:38,207
-What?
-How is he?

2250
01:32:38,242 --> 01:32:39,933
-He's all right.
We just make sure

2251
01:32:39,968 --> 01:32:41,694
you get up with everything
you fell down with.

2252
01:32:41,728 --> 01:32:43,834
-I found him next to
that flimsy plot device.

2253
01:32:43,868 --> 01:32:46,733
-Yeah, I was doing a beer bong
with the guys from Theta Chi.

2254
01:32:46,768 --> 01:32:50,047
-Hey! I found him!

2255
01:32:50,081 --> 01:32:51,531
That's quite a bump there, boy.

2256
01:32:51,566 --> 01:32:53,706
What happened? Huh?

2257
01:32:53,740 --> 01:32:56,053
-Darling, are you all right?

2258
01:32:56,087 --> 01:32:57,744
-You gave your mother
quite a scare.

2259
01:32:57,779 --> 01:32:58,883
-Yes.

2260
01:32:58,918 --> 01:33:00,195
-Here it was getting dark,
and no Johnny.

2261
01:33:00,229 --> 01:33:01,334
-You're alive?
-Yeah.

2262
01:33:01,368 --> 01:33:04,302
-Her, too?
-Mom, I've turned Hindu.

2263
01:33:04,337 --> 01:33:06,684
-Boy, was that a dream,
or was it?

2264
01:33:06,719 --> 01:33:08,686
-It was.
-Well, I must try to repay you

2265
01:33:08,721 --> 01:33:10,170
for all the trouble
you've gone to.

2266
01:33:10,205 --> 01:33:12,656
Won't you and your assistant
join us for dinner?

2267
01:33:12,690 --> 01:33:14,243
-Do.
-Done.

2268
01:33:14,278 --> 01:33:15,417
-Did.

2269
01:33:15,451 --> 01:33:17,833
-Will you play house with me
when we get home?

2270
01:33:17,868 --> 01:33:19,386
-Yes, we'll play house,
for God's sake!

2271
01:33:19,421 --> 01:33:21,043
Shut up!
-...well, all right,

2272
01:33:21,078 --> 01:33:23,425
but I got to keep an eye out
for Ro-Man.

2273
01:33:23,459 --> 01:33:25,876
-Really, Johnny, you're
overdoing this spaceman act.

2274
01:33:25,910 --> 01:33:26,980
-He's high.

2275
01:33:27,015 --> 01:33:28,533
-There simply aren't
any such things.

2276
01:33:28,568 --> 01:33:31,122
-Have you been in
